1
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:13,138
THE LOVE LAB

2
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:16,975
THE AFTERNOON
WHEN TWO COUPLES WENT ON DATES

3
00:00:18,935 --> 00:00:20,353
This place looks different.

4
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,938
-We should do a tea ceremony.
-Yeah.

5
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:24,816
-That color suits you.
-It does?

6
00:00:24,899 --> 00:00:26,025
Thanks.

7
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:28,028
I usually wear white,

8
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:30,071
but sometimes I wear bright colors.

9
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:31,823
Yeah, you do a good job of it.

10
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:34,034
You draw well too.

11
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:35,994
Come on. Don't make me blush.

12
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:38,329
-Wait.
-Do you want to eat something?

13
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:40,540
-Anything you need?
-Peppermint tea.

14
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:42,459
How do I get peppermint tea?

15
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:44,878
-There isn't any.
-I think,

16
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:46,921
we have to be able to leave.

17
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:48,173
We have to leave and…

18
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:52,761
Think of me when you see peppermint tea.

19
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:55,472
JOOHONEY, CHARLESENTER

20
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:57,390
Come on!

21
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:59,809
-Come on, Hye-won.
-I'm saving that comment.

22
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:02,145
Think of me when you drink hibiscus tea.

23
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:03,897
I'll remember it.

24
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,732
-You will?
-Yeah, I'll remember.

25
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:08,318
What the heck?

26
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:11,071
Think of me when you see peppermint tea.

27
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:12,655
I'll have to go get it.

28
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:15,784
I should think of you and pick it up.

29
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:18,078
-Do you like tea?
-Yeah.

30
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:20,914
I like herbal tea and fruit tea.

31
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:23,374
Do you like coffee more, Ha-yoon?

32
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:25,710
I do like coffee a lot.

33
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:26,753
Me too.

34
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:31,049
When I travel, I'd get coffee
from a place that's well-known there.

35
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:32,509
<i>Maybe you work at a cafe?</i>

36
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:34,052
WHILE THE TWO SHARE THEIR INTERESTS

37
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,680
Did you just take a picture of me?

38
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:40,391
So you like taking photos.

39
00:01:40,475 --> 00:01:41,601
Just making memories.

40
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:44,395
CASUALLY JOINS HIS SELFIE

41
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:45,563
<i>I have three chins.</i>

42
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:48,066
<i>It became a goofy photo.</i>

43
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:49,943
I'm making you shine, aren't I?

44
00:01:50,527 --> 00:01:52,320
Yeah, I like that.

45
00:01:53,988 --> 00:01:55,240
This is nice.

46
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,787
I kind of like this.

47
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:02,539
What do you like?

48
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:03,957
-Relaxing?
-Yeah.

49
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:09,671
It's perfect.

50
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,842
Hurry.

51
00:02:16,761 --> 00:02:17,929
GENTLY

52
00:02:18,012 --> 00:02:18,888
Peace.

53
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:21,516
What was that?

54
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,560
It took burst shots?

55
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:27,230
<i>-It looks cute.</i>
<i>-It's cute.</i>

56
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:30,233
SLIP

57
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,609
-This again?
-Thumbs up.

58
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:32,527
Heart.

59
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,003
At this rate, they made up their minds.

60
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:52,046
They took that photo
after making up their minds.

61
00:02:57,051 --> 00:02:58,136
What's up with that?

62
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:01,306
<i>That's so cute.</i>

63
00:03:03,349 --> 00:03:04,475
Should we light the fire?

64
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:11,399
Wow!

65
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:13,192
Awesome.

66
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:15,528
It's so pretty. Oh, my.

67
00:03:15,612 --> 00:03:18,781
You know, my hands are

68
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:21,200
-really cold.
-I know.

69
00:03:22,118 --> 00:03:23,494
I have cold hands and feet.

70
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:25,496
-Really?
-Yeah, it's really bad.

71
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:26,998
HOLDING IT TIGHT

72
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:29,375
-Right? Isn't it so bad?
-What's going on?

73
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:30,752
It's really bad.

74
00:03:30,835 --> 00:03:31,711
It's so cold.

75
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:33,755
It's so warm. I love it.

76
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:37,050
Let's go on a date.

77
00:03:37,842 --> 00:03:39,135
Date? I'd love that.

78
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:41,012
When will we get a chance?

79
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:43,014
-We'll get one, right?
-Will we?

80
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:45,308
-We have to make it happen.
-How? Will you become king?

81
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:46,559
I should become king.

82
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:50,688
-If I don't, I'll have to win their favor.
-Win their favor?

83
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:54,192
-What was your first impression of me?
-My first impression of you?

84
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:57,654
I thought we wouldn't have much in common.

85
00:03:57,737 --> 00:04:00,657
I thought I was really into looks

86
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:03,660
but after spending a lot of time with you,

87
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:06,246
I realized that I care
about the personality too.

88
00:04:06,329 --> 00:04:07,413
Wait. Hang on.

89
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:09,540
When you said you didn't care about looks…

90
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:15,171
No, looks used to play a huge part for me.

91
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:18,091
Whose looks did you like
the most at first?

92
00:04:18,174 --> 00:04:20,802
It's you. That's why I chose you at first.

93
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:22,053
-Really?
-Yeah.

94
00:04:22,136 --> 00:04:24,764
Are you curious about anyone else?

95
00:04:24,847 --> 00:04:25,974
Just you, for now.

96
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:27,684
There's nobody else besides you.

97
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:29,269
-Really?
-Yeah.

98
00:04:29,978 --> 00:04:31,062
For now, there's no one.

99
00:04:31,145 --> 00:04:32,730
-Okay.
-Yeah.

100
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:33,648
There's no one else.

101
00:04:33,731 --> 00:04:35,400
If I went back and voted again?

102
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:37,485
I'd vote for Jung-min.

103
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:39,445
I would've grabbed a handful
and never let go.

104
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:43,825
I think I was drawn to him more
through our conversations than his looks.

105
00:04:43,908 --> 00:04:48,162
At first, he acted more lively
to help break the ice

106
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:49,872
but he's also very quiet.

107
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:54,627
I realized he was trying hard
to make everyone feel comfortable.

108
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:58,131
After realizing that,
I became more attracted to him.

109
00:04:58,881 --> 00:05:00,091
I was thankful to you.

110
00:05:00,174 --> 00:05:02,093
Everyone felt awkward.

111
00:05:02,176 --> 00:05:05,388
It's hard to make such an effort.

112
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:07,307
Yeah, it's hard for me even now.

113
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,183
You were making an effort.

114
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:12,020
That's a strength. It's a good thing.

115
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:15,315
Did you see the photo booth message

116
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:17,692
-I worked really hard on?
-Yes.

117
00:05:17,775 --> 00:05:18,693
Why no reaction?

118
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:23,156
Did you really work hard on it?

119
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:24,782
At first…

120
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:27,285
-Yeah?
-No,

121
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:28,578
-I'd rather not say.
-Tell me.

122
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:29,537
I'll keep that to myself.

123
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:32,290
Date tomorrow?

124
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:34,667
I do want to go on a date tomorrow.

125
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:36,169
I asked who you wanted to go with.

126
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:37,962
Right, who would I go with?

127
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:42,550
I hope I become king.

128
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:44,677
Are you trying to win my favor?

129
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:45,636
No.

130
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,597
You never mentioned it, did you?

131
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,974
-What?
-What does your ideal type look like?

132
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:51,142
Do you have one?

133
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:52,602
My ideal type?

134
00:05:53,102 --> 00:05:54,687
I like someone who has fair skin,

135
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:56,814
someone who's short rather than tall,

136
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,941
and I like long, straight hair.

137
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:01,152
Long, black, straight hair.

138
00:06:01,235 --> 00:06:02,278
Someone who's pretty?

139
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:04,030
I like a pretty woman.

140
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:05,573
Someone who's pretty and cute.

141
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:08,659
What is your ideal type?

142
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:12,455
Someone with a good first impression?

143
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:15,833
A good… How should I put it?

144
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:18,086
I got a bit nervous

145
00:06:18,711 --> 00:06:20,088
and felt embarrassed,

146
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:22,381
<i>so I acted a bit awkward.</i>

147
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:23,883
I was going to say something nice.

148
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:28,012
-Yeah?
-You became quiet.

149
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:31,474
<i>I did feel awkward,</i>

150
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:35,770
but I really felt shy more than anything.

151
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:40,191
It was our first date,
so I wanted to impress her.

152
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:43,027
I didn't want to show her my shy side.

153
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:46,405
<i>I think I tried very hard</i>
<i>not to show that side of me.</i>

154
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:47,323
What is it?

155
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:50,743
To be more exact,

156
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:53,996
I thought you looked like
someone I'd be attracted to.

157
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,040
-Really?
-Yeah.

158
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,417
We met up with the staff, right?

159
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:00,336
-You told them your type, right?
-Yeah.

160
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:04,882
I like someone
who has fair skin and is skinny.

161
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:07,218
I like someone
who kind of looks like a baby fox.

162
00:07:07,301 --> 00:07:08,886
Like the actor Lee Jong-suk?

163
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:12,640
They brought someone who looked
exactly like the guy I described.

164
00:07:14,934 --> 00:07:16,102
-Hello.
-Hello.

165
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:17,103
Hello.

166
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:20,815
-Can I sit…
-Please sit wherever you'd like.

167
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:28,281
I see it.

168
00:07:29,198 --> 00:07:31,617
Even though you're isolated
with your ideal type,

169
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:35,246
-it may not work out.
-We know it may not.

170
00:07:35,329 --> 00:07:36,581
It may not work out.

171
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:39,292
As soon as I saw you, I started laughing.

172
00:07:39,876 --> 00:07:42,670
How could they find
someone who looks like that?

173
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:44,964
It was so surprising

174
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,591
<i>to the point that it made me laugh.</i>

175
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:53,389
Yeah.

176
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:56,309
Let's stop here.

177
00:07:56,893 --> 00:07:58,853
The ocean's beautiful.

178
00:07:58,936 --> 00:08:01,397
Yeah, the mountain is tall.

179
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:02,982
-Hello.
-Hello.

180
00:08:03,065 --> 00:08:04,025
Hello.

181
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:04,984
Where should we sit?

182
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:06,235
Eat the fried dish first.

183
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,153
-Okay.
-Okay.

184
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:14,577
To be honest,
I never had marinated crab before.

185
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:17,246
-Really?
-Tell me how to eat it.

186
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,998
You just grab it

187
00:08:19,081 --> 00:08:20,708
and suck the meat out.

188
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:24,128
-It's good if you mix it with rice.
-Mix it with rice?

189
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:26,631
This is too challenging.

190
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:28,007
This is like an experiment.

191
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:31,719
Can they eat messy like this
and still be attracted to each other?

192
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:33,262
-We are the Love Lab.
-Yeah.

193
00:08:33,346 --> 00:08:35,306
-It's like that.
-We even experiment on eating.

194
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:38,518
Just suck the meat out.

195
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:43,314
-It's good.
-How is it?

196
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:45,900
I've never seen anyone
eat marinated crabs so cutely like that.

197
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:46,984
"It's good."

198
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:49,612
I want to act like
I never had marinated crabs either.

199
00:08:49,695 --> 00:08:50,530
Give it a shot.

200
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:51,489
-Give it a shot?
-Yeah.

201
00:08:51,572 --> 00:08:53,032
-But--
-You want to look cute.

202
00:08:53,115 --> 00:08:55,743
I've never seen this before. What is it?

203
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:58,746
Take a small bite and say,

204
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:00,331
"It's good." Then--

205
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:01,791
-It's cute.
-Really?

206
00:09:01,874 --> 00:09:03,834
-Yeah.
-I'll say, "It's good."

207
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:06,462
Then, after he goes to the bathroom,
I'll gobble it up.

208
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,883
It's definitely good.

209
00:09:12,176 --> 00:09:13,678
-It's good.
-How is it?

210
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:14,845
-Isn't it good?
-Yeah.

211
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:17,014
-It comes out when you press it.
-Okay.

212
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:18,057
It's really good.

213
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:19,183
Okay.

214
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,608
It can look a little funny.

215
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:28,526
I know.

216
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:36,117
REVEAL YOUR AGE AND JOB NOW

217
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,243
Tell me what it is.

218
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:39,704
Age and job? All of a sudden?

219
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:41,122
-Here?
-While eating crabs?

220
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:43,916
But it's so out of the blue, isn't it?

221
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,168
Why reveal their jobs
while eating marinated crabs?

222
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:48,963
I really don't get the timing
of revealing one's age and job

223
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:51,340
-on our show, the Love Lab.
-Right?

224
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:56,137
How old are you?

225
00:09:56,887 --> 00:09:58,931
You kept on thinking I was older.

226
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:02,143
How old you do I look?

227
00:10:02,893 --> 00:10:05,896
Since you thought I was older,

228
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,024
I do think you're young,

229
00:10:08,107 --> 00:10:09,233
so maybe 25?

230
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:13,112
Can't you go first?

231
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:15,531
-I'm 26 years old.
-26 years old?

232
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:16,616
I was born in 2001.

233
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:18,409
-Born in 2001.
-2001. Okay.

234
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:19,702
He's the same age as my younger sibling.

235
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:20,745
Really?

236
00:10:20,828 --> 00:10:21,954
Yeah, he's the same age.

237
00:10:22,038 --> 00:10:23,122
There's a huge age gap.

238
00:10:23,205 --> 00:10:24,415
Yeah, we're seven years apart.

239
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:28,502
<i>I was worried that</i>
<i>he might think I was too young</i>

240
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:31,297
and feel a bit uncomfortable with me.

241
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:32,423
Are we the same age?

242
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:33,507
No.

243
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:34,508
Am I older?

244
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:35,593
Yes.

245
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:36,510
Are you 24?

246
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,389
How much younger is okay for you?

247
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:43,434
Me? Not 20 years old…

248
00:10:43,934 --> 00:10:45,144
I'm 22.

249
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:46,145
22 years old?

250
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:48,272
Born in 2005?

251
00:10:48,356 --> 00:10:49,482
That's my little sibling's age!

252
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:50,983
Your little sibling and mine?

253
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:52,818
I'm 22.

254
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:53,778
22 years old?

255
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:56,489
22 years old?

256
00:10:57,907 --> 00:11:00,493
Unbelievable.
Of course, you thought I was older.

257
00:11:01,118 --> 00:11:02,828
You were born in 2001, right?

258
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:06,999
I don't think that's a huge age gap.

259
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:09,293
But you said you were 25.

260
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:12,421
I thought you'd be around my age.

261
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:13,589
22 years old?

262
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:15,716
Unbelievable.

263
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:18,344
Four years isn't a huge gap though.

264
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,722
22 years old?

265
00:11:21,806 --> 00:11:22,973
We're done for.

266
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:24,558
-We're done for?
-Yeah.

267
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:25,643
There's no reason for that.

268
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:29,563
My job is…

269
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:30,689
Wait, try to guess it.

270
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:32,024
Don't you want to guess?

271
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,485
-You must want to guess since you're 22.
-Give me one…

272
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:36,362
That's such a stereotype.

273
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,782
You're right. I agree.

274
00:11:39,865 --> 00:11:41,659
-What is it?
-I am

275
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,495
a dancer. I do ballet.

276
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:45,746
-For real?
-Yeah.

277
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:47,081
I'm a ballet dancer.

278
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:48,707
-For real?
-Yeah.

279
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:52,461
<i>I'm a ballerino.</i>

280
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:56,132
<i>I studied practical dance</i>
<i>at Korea National University of Arts,</i>

281
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:59,552
<i>and currently, I am a dancer</i>
<i>with Yunbyul Ballet Company.</i>

282
00:12:01,887 --> 00:12:05,141
<i>I achieved the second place</i>
<i>on a male dancer survival show.</i>

283
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:06,058
RUNNER-UP ON MNET'S "STAGE FIGHTER"

284
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:10,062
Ballerinos must express
their emotions very well.

285
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:13,357
<i>There are at least 1,000 seats</i>
<i>in the auditorium.</i>

286
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,109
<i>I have to show the audience who I am</i>

287
00:12:15,192 --> 00:12:17,528
<i>and become fully immersed</i>
<i>in my performance.</i>

288
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:24,577
<i>To give a flawless performance,</i>
<i>I keep pushing myself and train offstage.</i>

289
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:32,376
<i>When I deliver a deeply moving experience</i>
<i>to the audience on stage, I feel happy.</i>

290
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:36,589
KANG KYUNG-HO
26 YEARS OLD, BALLET DANCER

291
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:40,885
I am a ballet dancer.

292
00:12:40,968 --> 00:12:42,428
<i>At that moment,</i>

293
00:12:42,511 --> 00:12:46,765
I felt like my eyes turned into hearts.

294
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:47,892
-Interesting, right?
-Yes.

295
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:50,102
-I don't look like a ballerino, do I?
-No.

296
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:51,896
Everyone says that.

297
00:12:51,979 --> 00:12:54,064
He has fair skin, he's slim,

298
00:12:54,148 --> 00:12:56,442
and I love that he has fox eyes.

299
00:12:57,026 --> 00:13:00,613
He has a really beautiful body line.

300
00:13:00,696 --> 00:13:02,531
I like people who are in the arts.

301
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:05,409
On top of that, I like sly men.

302
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:08,078
After finding out what he does for work,

303
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:12,166
I totally fell head over heels for him.

304
00:13:13,792 --> 00:13:16,045
How did you end up doing ballet?

305
00:13:16,128 --> 00:13:17,838
Did you see that?

306
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:20,007
She's so excited. Look at her feet.

307
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,010
-She's bouncing them.
-Yeah.

308
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:24,011
She's so excited.

309
00:13:24,094 --> 00:13:25,054
How did you catch that?

310
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:28,057
How did you end up doing ballet?

311
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:30,267
My little sister started it first.

312
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:32,603
I naturally ended up doing it too.

313
00:13:34,021 --> 00:13:35,731
What do you do for work?

314
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:37,525
I'm studying philosophy.

315
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:38,692
Philosophy?

316
00:13:39,568 --> 00:13:42,655
Philosophy is less about finding answers

317
00:13:42,738 --> 00:13:45,157
and more about asking "why."

318
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:48,327
<i>I'm majoring in Philosophy</i>
<i>at Sogang University.</i>

319
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:50,120
Sogang University?

320
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:51,288
That's insane.

321
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:53,249
-She looks even prettier now.
-Wow.

322
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:56,502
<i>Ever since I was young,</i>
<i>I've loved theater and musicals,</i>

323
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:59,421
<i>so I set my goal of becoming</i>
<i>a performance arts producer.</i>

324
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:02,174
<i>I felt that producing performances</i>
<i>for a broad audience</i>

325
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:04,677
<i>required deeper thinking.</i>

326
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:07,972
<i>That's why I chose philosophy.</i>

327
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:11,308
<i>By taking on roles in planning,</i>
<i>production, directing,</i>

328
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:13,435
<i>and every stage of theater</i>
<i>through my drama club,</i>

329
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:17,064
<i>I'm steadily working toward my goal</i>
<i>of becoming a performing arts producer.</i>

330
00:14:17,147 --> 00:14:20,359
LEE YE-RIM
22 YEARS OLD, PHILOSOPHY MAJOR AT SOGANG

331
00:14:20,442 --> 00:14:21,694
-Philosophy?
-Yes.

332
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:23,654
Honestly, that isn't so shocking.

333
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,239
But you're 22.

334
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:26,699
You have to be nice.

335
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:28,409
-Me?
-Yes.

336
00:14:28,492 --> 00:14:30,327
Shouldn't you be nice to me?

337
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:31,704
Like respecting the elderly?

338
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:32,621
Yes.

339
00:14:33,205 --> 00:14:35,291
Didn't you say that we're done for?

340
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,334
You seemed caught off guard.

341
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:41,213
I was caught off guard. I didn't think
a 22-year-old would be here.

342
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:46,719
<i>This may sound a bit strange.</i>

343
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:47,678
I…

344
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:52,349
I don't care about whether she is
younger, older, or the same age.

345
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:56,020
But if someone overlaps with
my younger sister's age,

346
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:57,688
I strangely become distant.

347
00:14:57,771 --> 00:15:00,441
It's not the deciding factor,

348
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:04,820
but the moment I heard her age,
I think I put a small barrier between us.

349
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:10,034
Kyung-ho's little sister and Ye-rim
are the same age?

350
00:15:11,452 --> 00:15:12,786
So what?

351
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:14,288
It does matter.

352
00:15:14,371 --> 00:15:15,331
How come?

353
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:18,667
You start thinking she is
your younger sister,

354
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:22,796
so you'll want to take care of her
and say things like, "Do better."

355
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:26,926
I think that same frame has been
put on Ye-rim now too.

356
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:28,802
Okay. But you know,

357
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:31,388
it could be because she is
exactly the same age as his sister

358
00:15:31,472 --> 00:15:32,890
and not younger or anything.

359
00:15:32,973 --> 00:15:35,267
-I can't date someone my brother's age.
-Exactly.

360
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:40,314
<i>I felt like there was</i>
<i>a bit of distance between us.</i>

361
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:41,899
What did I do when I was 22?

362
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:44,276
Are you trying to put distance between us?

363
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,653
What did I do?

364
00:15:46,236 --> 00:15:50,324
I really have felt that age
is only a number.

365
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:53,619
-But you didn't react that way.
-Me?

366
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:57,498
But the number two and two
is a bit shocking.

367
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:02,920
I think 24 was the youngest I've dated,

368
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:06,298
so I never even considered
anyone younger than that.

369
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:10,803
Honestly,
I didn't think a student could be on this

370
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:12,638
because of various circumstances.

371
00:16:12,721 --> 00:16:14,556
Has he never watched dating shows?

372
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,767
There's always a college student
on dating shows.

373
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:18,978
I took some time off.

374
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:19,979
Really?

375
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,982
I like that you made that choice.

376
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:24,775
Stop talking like an old-timer.

377
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:29,613
I really admire that kind of decisiveness.

378
00:16:31,073 --> 00:16:32,491
-Shall we clink our glasses?
-Yeah.

379
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:43,544
Chae-rin asked you
that question yesterday.

380
00:16:43,627 --> 00:16:47,047
-What?
-How many people you are interested in.

381
00:16:47,631 --> 00:16:49,550
How many would you like to get to know?

382
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:50,759
Me?

383
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:51,927
Right now?

384
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:53,804
Right now, there are two.

385
00:16:53,887 --> 00:16:55,514
<i>I was a bit annoyed.</i>

386
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:58,308
But it should be that way.

387
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:00,728
And the reason why

388
00:17:00,811 --> 00:17:03,313
we are all interested in someone

389
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:06,442
is just because of the first impression,
so we don't know how it'll change.

390
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:09,695
That was the conclusion everybody came to.

391
00:17:09,778 --> 00:17:10,988
<i>But…</i>

392
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:15,576
<i>"I don't get that"</i>
<i>was </i><i>what</i> I <i>was </i><i>thinking.</i>

393
00:17:15,659 --> 00:17:16,869
Can I ask who it is?

394
00:17:16,952 --> 00:17:18,078
No, you can't.

395
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:20,581
-Want me to tell you?
-Yes.

396
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,500
The person I'm interested in?

397
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:24,752
First of all, you.

398
00:17:29,423 --> 00:17:30,549
Are you curious?

399
00:17:30,632 --> 00:17:31,467
Yes.

400
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:35,846
I was most curious about you.

401
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:39,975
Honestly, I'm curious about everyone.

402
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:45,189
<i>I didn't want to fully reveal</i>
<i>what was in my heart.</i>

403
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:47,566
<i>I just want to say nice things to others.</i>

404
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:50,694
<i>If you don't,</i>
<i>both parties would feel awkward.</i>

405
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,073
Am I even allowed to say?

406
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:55,449
It's…

407
00:17:57,159 --> 00:17:58,452
Ga-yeon.

408
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:04,875
-But Ga-yeon is so different from her.
-Right.

409
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:06,752
They are polar opposites.

410
00:18:06,835 --> 00:18:07,669
She must be nervous.

411
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:09,963
-She must be.
-And she seems older.

412
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:11,924
Oh, no. So it begins.

413
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:14,843
She knows that she's younger too now.

414
00:18:14,927 --> 00:18:17,888
The whirlwind of emotions
is about to begin.

415
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:20,265
Yesterday, I was curious about

416
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:21,809
you and Ga-yeon.

417
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:24,561
Why?

418
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:27,898
What about you?

419
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:28,982
Never mind.

420
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:35,364
Why are you laughing?

421
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:37,074
Because it's funny.

422
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:38,742
What's funny?

423
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:40,285
The fact that you're 22 years old.

424
00:18:40,869 --> 00:18:41,870
I'm just kidding.

425
00:18:43,455 --> 00:18:45,833
I'm just kidding. It was a joke.

426
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,627
It can be funny.

427
00:18:49,628 --> 00:18:50,462
Why did you laugh?

428
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:53,632
I laughed because it was what I expected.

429
00:18:53,715 --> 00:18:56,635
-The two people you were curious about.
-I see.

430
00:18:56,718 --> 00:19:00,430
I do think that
I acted pretty transparently.

431
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:04,101
I don't think I spoke to anybody
besides you two.

432
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:07,604
I felt nervous rather than secure.

433
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:10,732
When I asked him a question,

434
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:16,697
I knew that I wouldn't get a reaction
to the extent that I would expect.

435
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:21,368
So it was hard for me
to ask questions to draw him out.

436
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:23,078
You know,

437
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:25,164
I realized what I don't like
about how Kyung-ho acts.

438
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:28,417
If he isn't sure of how he feels
and can't answer directly,

439
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:29,585
why would he do this?

440
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:32,880
To be honest, that was
because he didn't know her age

441
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:35,757
and he just followed his heart.

442
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:37,384
I think that's understandable.

443
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:38,802
How understanding of you.

444
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:41,346
He can do things like this.
It's understandable.

445
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:42,472
He didn't know her age.

446
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:43,932
That's not how women feel.

447
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:46,185
Usually, I'm not that honest

448
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:47,853
and I don't open up easily.

449
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:51,148
That's why it's very hard
for me to force myself to do it

450
00:19:51,231 --> 00:19:52,649
since I'm not used to doing it.

451
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:55,819
Let's say I become the king.

452
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,654
I can choose who I want to date.

453
00:19:57,738 --> 00:20:00,073
Would you like me to choose you or not?

454
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:01,867
I'd love it if you chose me.

455
00:20:02,826 --> 00:20:06,413
You might want to talk to
someone other than me.

456
00:20:06,496 --> 00:20:09,458
I do want to talk to someone else too
since we don't have a lot of time.

457
00:20:09,541 --> 00:20:10,417
Exactly.

458
00:20:11,293 --> 00:20:12,336
What about you?

459
00:20:13,378 --> 00:20:14,838
Are you going to choose me again?

460
00:20:14,922 --> 00:20:17,507
Would my answer change your answer?

461
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,218
Me?

462
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:22,346
No, it would be nice if you voted for me.

463
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:24,056
-Why?
-What?

464
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:25,474
Because you voted for me.

465
00:20:25,557 --> 00:20:26,808
Well…

466
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:28,602
You'd be happy with anybody's votes.

467
00:20:28,685 --> 00:20:30,771
No, that's not true.

468
00:20:30,854 --> 00:20:34,316
I didn't get the feeling that
he was happy it was me.

469
00:20:34,399 --> 00:20:37,986
I felt like he didn't feel
the same way about me.

470
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:39,780
And what do you… Wait, no.

471
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:41,698
How do you feel…

472
00:20:44,493 --> 00:20:46,912
I think those questions
are very difficult.

473
00:20:46,995 --> 00:20:48,830
"How do you feel?"

474
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:50,707
"What are you going to do tomorrow?"

475
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:52,709
The fact that she asked me those questions

476
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:54,711
came across as being very honest,

477
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:57,130
<i>but it did make me feel uncomfortable too.</i>

478
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:03,387
I think it would be premature
to make a decision right now.

479
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:05,222
Of course.

480
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:06,515
-It's their first date.
-Yeah.

481
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:09,851
Those questions are like the ones you ask
before the final decision.

482
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:11,353
Ye-rim likes him so much.

483
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:13,355
-She just wants to go ahead with it.
-Right.

484
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:15,065
Her ideal type is Kyung-ho.

485
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:17,276
One is smitten, the other isn't.

486
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:19,987
But Kyung-ho only put
one Heart Chip in in the beginning,

487
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:22,698
that tells me that he's not the type

488
00:21:22,781 --> 00:21:26,702
-to go all-in from the start.
-Right.

489
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:29,329
It wasn't clear who had
the upper hand before.

490
00:21:29,413 --> 00:21:32,624
-But now, it feels like Ye-rim…
-That's it.

491
00:21:32,708 --> 00:21:34,960
-…is clinging to him.
-Yes, it seems that way.

492
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:37,713
<i>What about you?</i>

493
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:40,299
-Oh, no. Ye-rim looks upset.
<i>-Would you ask me out?</i>

494
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:42,884
The mood turned serious already.

495
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:45,512
-The air.
-Yeah, the air feels heavy.

496
00:21:45,595 --> 00:21:47,097
It's too soon to be like this.

497
00:21:47,639 --> 00:21:48,598
What about you?

498
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,143
Would you ask me out?

499
00:21:52,019 --> 00:21:52,894
Yes.

500
00:22:04,031 --> 00:22:05,907
You aren't curious about anyone else?

501
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:09,119
Someone you want to talk to.

502
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:12,706
I think it's more meaningful for me

503
00:22:13,332 --> 00:22:16,835
to spend time with someone
I am even a little more interested in.

504
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:19,963
Understood.

505
00:22:22,758 --> 00:22:25,343
I thought our feelings would at least be

506
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:28,513
somewhat similar
in terms of pace or intensity,

507
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:30,348
but I don't think that was the case.

508
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:32,100
The thing is,

509
00:22:32,934 --> 00:22:35,604
if my feelings weren’t strong,

510
00:22:35,687 --> 00:22:38,815
<i>I don’t think I would</i>
<i>say these things or act this way.</i>

511
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:41,693
<i>But he could easily do it</i>
<i>even though he doesn't feel that strongly.</i>

512
00:22:41,777 --> 00:22:43,195
Because she's pretty.

513
00:22:45,197 --> 00:22:48,617
I guess I misunderstood
and misread the situation.

514
00:22:49,284 --> 00:22:51,745
