00:34:22,143 --> 00:34:23,603
Are you an actor?

774
00:34:23,686 --> 00:34:25,021
Is that the art field you're in?

775
00:34:26,272 --> 00:34:28,191
-That's right.
-Stop lying.

776
00:34:28,274 --> 00:34:29,567
-Are you for real?
-Yeah, I'm serious.

777
00:34:30,777 --> 00:34:32,612
-What? For real?
-I'm in acting.

778
00:34:34,989 --> 00:34:36,157
-Really?
-Yeah.

779
00:34:37,825 --> 00:34:38,785
He's an actor.

780
00:34:39,452 --> 00:34:40,369
It doesn't suit him.

781
00:34:40,453 --> 00:34:42,997
-I think it suits him.
-He seems introverted.

782
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:44,123
He's more attractive now.

783
00:34:45,124 --> 00:34:48,336
<i>I am majoring in Theater and Film</i>
<i>at Dongguk University.</i>

784
00:34:49,754 --> 00:34:53,341
<i>I have loved dancing and being on stage</i>
<i>since I was young.</i>

785
00:34:53,424 --> 00:34:55,301
<i>I'm pursuing my dream of becoming an actor</i>

786
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:58,221
<i>by connecting with audiences</i>
<i>through the stage of theater.</i>

787
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:01,849
<i>During my military service,</i>
<i>I joined the Army performance team</i>

788
00:35:01,933 --> 00:35:04,811
<i>and gained attention for performing</i>
<i>the opening part of "like JENNIE."</i>

789
00:35:07,021 --> 00:35:11,025
<i>That experience inspired me to </i><i>pursue</i>
<i>my passion </i><i>for </i><i>the </i><i>stage </i><i>even </i><i>further.</i>

790
00:35:15,905 --> 00:35:16,739
What?

791
00:35:16,823 --> 00:35:18,282
I didn't expect that.

792
00:35:18,366 --> 00:35:19,784
He's practically a con artist.

793
00:35:20,284 --> 00:35:22,370
<i>Now, I hope to become an actor</i>

794
00:35:22,453 --> 00:35:25,289
<i>who continues to deepen his craft</i>
<i>through diverse experiences.</i>

795
00:35:25,832 --> 00:35:28,543
PARK DO-GEON
24 YEARS OLD, THEATER AND FILM MAJOR

796
00:35:29,127 --> 00:35:31,504
You may have seen me
while scrolling through Reels.

797
00:35:31,587 --> 00:35:33,631
-While scrolling through Reels?
-Yeah.

798
00:35:33,714 --> 00:35:34,924
It was when I was a soldier.

799
00:35:35,007 --> 00:35:35,925
Isn't it something

800
00:35:36,008 --> 00:35:38,302
like those people who dance
in the military?

801
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:41,931
Like a dance video
of "Hype Boy" or something.

802
00:35:42,682 --> 00:35:43,933
It's Jennie's…

803
00:35:44,016 --> 00:35:44,976
Wait, Jennie?

804
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:47,061
-"like JENNIE."
-"like JENNIE."

805
00:35:47,562 --> 00:35:49,021
-Did you see it?
-I did.

806
00:35:49,105 --> 00:35:50,189
Really?

807
00:35:50,273 --> 00:35:51,774
-You were in that?
-Yeah.

808
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:53,234
I'm the one in the beginning.

809
00:35:56,279 --> 00:35:58,114
-Really?
-In the intro.

810
00:35:59,407 --> 00:36:00,241
Amazing.

811
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:03,703
Are you good at dancing too?

812
00:36:03,786 --> 00:36:05,705
I took some lessons a while back

813
00:36:05,788 --> 00:36:07,123
for about two to three years.

814
00:36:07,206 --> 00:36:08,416
I knew it.

815
00:36:08,499 --> 00:36:10,710
-You have the body of someone like that.
-Really?

816
00:36:11,210 --> 00:36:12,628
I want to see it again.

817
00:36:13,212 --> 00:36:16,090
I was a bit disappointed.

818
00:36:16,174 --> 00:36:19,177
I wanted to avoid anybody
in the arts and sports field.

819
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:20,928
So it was a bit disappointing.

820
00:36:21,012 --> 00:36:23,139
But I was hoping he'd be an athlete.

821
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:26,767
Even though he'd be in arts and sports,
an athlete might have been okay.

822
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:28,728
That thought did go through my mind.

823
00:36:28,811 --> 00:36:30,146
"Okay, he's an athlete."

824
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:34,066
I guess I was hoping or imagined
that he was one.

825
00:36:34,567 --> 00:36:39,947
It made me take a step back
and view him more objectively

826
00:36:40,031 --> 00:36:40,990
in that moment.

827
00:36:41,699 --> 00:36:42,825
Show some respect to me.

828
00:36:44,869 --> 00:36:46,204
Man.

829
00:36:47,330 --> 00:36:48,247
Show some respect.

830
00:36:53,127 --> 00:36:54,003
Can't say the words?

831
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:57,340
I'm curious.

832
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:02,762
So shocked.

833
00:37:05,014 --> 00:37:06,557
I've never dated a younger guy.

834
00:37:10,353 --> 00:37:12,355
I don't think it'll be too different.

835
00:37:13,022 --> 00:37:14,899
-Really?
-It may even be better.

836
00:37:21,447 --> 00:37:25,159
I've never been interested
in someone who's younger than me.

837
00:37:27,411 --> 00:37:28,537
Isn't that too direct?

838
00:37:28,621 --> 00:37:31,040
It's very discouraging to Do-geon.

839
00:37:31,123 --> 00:37:32,583
She went too far.

840
00:37:32,667 --> 00:37:34,001
But there are people like her.

841
00:37:34,085 --> 00:37:36,837
They don't even consider someone younger.

842
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:40,216
I want to round up everyone like that
and give them a real attitude adjustment.

843
00:37:41,008 --> 00:37:42,802
-But--
-So what if they're younger?

844
00:37:42,885 --> 00:37:45,846
They had a change of heart
just like Kyung-ho and Ye-rim.

845
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:47,014
I don't get it though.

846
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:48,557
She saw him as a man before.

847
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:49,600
But now she doesn't?

848
00:37:49,684 --> 00:37:50,977
She didn't know his age then.

849
00:37:51,060 --> 00:37:53,271
That dislike is totally unfounded.

850
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:54,897
Why would you dislike someone younger?

851
00:37:55,481 --> 00:37:59,151
I've never been interested
in someone who's younger than me.

852
00:38:00,069 --> 00:38:00,903
Honestly.

853
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:03,239
No interest in someone who's younger?

854
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:07,785
I've never viewed younger guys as men.

855
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:13,249
Is she putting up a wall between us

856
00:38:13,332 --> 00:38:15,209
or is she rejecting me?

857
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:18,754
Those thoughts did cross my mind.

858
00:38:19,338 --> 00:38:22,717
Either way, I could get her

859
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:27,054
to like me eventually.
That's the main thought I had.

860
00:38:27,638 --> 00:38:29,890
<i>So I wasn't too shaken by it.</i>

861
00:38:32,518 --> 00:38:33,769
I may be different.

862
00:38:37,898 --> 00:38:40,026
-He's determined to win her over.
-Let's go!

863
00:38:40,109 --> 00:38:41,819
-Yes!
-Just go for it!

864
00:38:41,902 --> 00:38:43,279
He's competitive. What a man!

865
00:38:43,362 --> 00:38:45,489
"I may be different."

866
00:38:46,574 --> 00:38:48,743
Yeah, you may be different.

867
00:38:49,368 --> 00:38:50,369
Show me you're different.

868
00:38:50,453 --> 00:38:53,122
THEIR SECRETS HAVE BEEN REVEALED

869
00:38:53,205 --> 00:38:55,041
Since we're sharing it…

870
00:38:55,124 --> 00:38:56,959
Wow! For real?

871
00:38:57,043 --> 00:38:58,627
I started over then.

872
00:38:59,253 --> 00:39:00,504
We must be getting a mission.

873
00:39:00,588 --> 00:39:01,797
-What is it?
-There it is.

874
00:39:01,881 --> 00:39:02,715
A LETTER ARRIVES

875
00:39:04,050 --> 00:39:05,634
-There's something.
-What is it?

876
00:39:05,718 --> 00:39:07,011
There's something.

877
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:09,638
-Ha-yoon is excited.
-Right?

878
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:10,848
It's his first time.

879
00:39:10,931 --> 00:39:12,725
-Why are you so happy about it?
-Ha-yoon.

880
00:39:12,808 --> 00:39:14,643
So this is how it feels.

881
00:39:15,227 --> 00:39:16,645
What is it? I'm nervous.

882
00:39:16,729 --> 00:39:18,564
This only applies to use four, right?

883
00:39:18,647 --> 00:39:20,775
I know. Doesn't it seem so special?

884
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:23,736
"A new chip has been added today.

885
00:39:23,819 --> 00:39:25,988
Go to the Heart Room
and check it out now."

886
00:39:26,072 --> 00:39:27,531
-What?
-A new chip?

887
00:39:28,866 --> 00:39:30,743
-And?
-That's it.

888
00:39:30,826 --> 00:39:31,911
-What?
-Let's go.

889
00:39:31,994 --> 00:39:32,912
What's going on?

890
00:39:32,995 --> 00:39:34,789
So there's something new.

891
00:39:36,165 --> 00:39:37,458
What's this?

892
00:39:40,628 --> 00:39:42,505
<i>A new chip has been added.</i>

893
00:39:44,882 --> 00:39:46,300
-Black?
-Black chips?

894
00:39:47,676 --> 00:39:51,347
<i>"Each person gets 10 Black Heart Chips."</i>

895
00:39:51,430 --> 00:39:56,477
<i>"This is a negative Heart Chip</i>
<i>that reduces your opponent's Heart Chips."</i>

896
00:39:57,061 --> 00:40:00,773
<i>"You may use it to hold back</i>
<i>someone you don't want as king."</i>

897
00:40:00,856 --> 00:40:04,110
<i>"Black Heart Chips may be used on anybody</i>

898
00:40:04,693 --> 00:40:06,570
<i>and can be used on multiple people."</i>

899
00:40:07,154 --> 00:40:10,574
<i>If you have used up</i>
<i>all 10 Black Heart Chips,</i>

900
00:40:10,658 --> 00:40:14,495
<i>you may exchange your Heart Chips</i>
<i>to get more Black Heart Chips.</i>

901
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:19,083
<i>"If you want to exchange it,</i>
<i>put your Heart Chips in the glass vase</i>

902
00:40:19,166 --> 00:40:22,128
<i>-and take the Black Heart Chips."</i>
<i>-I exchange it with mine, right?</i>

903
00:40:22,753 --> 00:40:24,630
-Wow.
-Negative Heart Chips.

904
00:40:24,713 --> 00:40:26,966
So they can use their own Heart Chips?

905
00:40:27,049 --> 00:40:28,509
To get additional Black ones.

906
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:33,222
<i>The Heart Chips in your Heart Box</i>
<i>resets every day.</i>

907
00:40:33,722 --> 00:40:35,057
How should I use them?

908
00:40:35,141 --> 00:40:36,767
How can I use them wisely?

909
00:40:36,851 --> 00:40:38,853
It's different from a regular vote.

910
00:40:38,936 --> 00:40:40,646
There must be a strategic way to use it.

911
00:40:40,729 --> 00:40:44,817
<i>There must be a reason why</i>
<i>this was revealed to us four first.</i>

912
00:40:45,317 --> 00:40:47,153
So how are we supposed to use these…

913
00:40:47,236 --> 00:40:51,532
-Preventing someone from becoming king.
-You can use it on a few people.

914
00:40:51,615 --> 00:40:52,825
You can do that with these.

915
00:40:52,908 --> 00:40:53,993
Get rid of their hearts.

916
00:40:54,076 --> 00:40:55,661
We can make someone king.

917
00:40:55,744 --> 00:40:56,579
-Right.
-I guess?

918
00:40:56,662 --> 00:40:59,623
-Since the king is made by other people.
-Right.

919
00:40:59,707 --> 00:41:01,667
If someone's a strong candidate,

920
00:41:01,750 --> 00:41:03,711
-we add ours to…
-If we wanted to,

921
00:41:03,794 --> 00:41:06,172
we could just trade Heart Chips
and reuse them.

922
00:41:06,255 --> 00:41:07,673
We already got ten to begin with.

923
00:41:07,756 --> 00:41:11,343
We can use underhanded tactics
by working together.

924
00:41:11,427 --> 00:41:12,553
We can definitely do that.

925
00:41:12,636 --> 00:41:14,346
Those people don't know about this.

926
00:41:14,430 --> 00:41:17,308
-They'll say, "What's this?"
-We're on the same boat.

927
00:41:17,391 --> 00:41:18,934
-The game is on.
-It's a secret.

928
00:41:19,018 --> 00:41:21,187
Let's plan it out and make it happen.

929
00:41:21,937 --> 00:41:22,771
It's possible.

930
00:41:22,855 --> 00:41:24,106
We could give each other hearts.

931
00:41:24,190 --> 00:41:26,901
You could give it to the person you want
in order to make them the king.

932
00:41:26,984 --> 00:41:29,153
-Yeah, we could.
-We could also discuss among ourselves.

933
00:41:29,236 --> 00:41:30,738
We have to conspire.

934
00:41:30,821 --> 00:41:31,822
HEART CHIPS BECAME TOOLS FOR POWER

935
00:41:31,906 --> 00:41:35,534
You know, I'd be offended
if I didn't get any Black Heart Chips.

936
00:41:35,618 --> 00:41:37,495
Do I not seem popular to you?

937
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:39,246
They must not think I can become king.

938
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:40,998
This is tough.

939
00:41:41,081 --> 00:41:42,291
These things are so hard.

940
00:41:42,958 --> 00:41:44,793
You know what I want to know?

941
00:41:44,877 --> 00:41:47,922
Is there a reason why we have to
do all this to make someone king?

942
00:41:48,506 --> 00:41:50,466
If one of the other four becomes king,

943
00:41:50,549 --> 00:41:53,677
the four of us may not
be able to go on a date again.

944
00:41:53,761 --> 00:41:56,972
-Then, one of us should become king.
-If we become king,

945
00:41:57,056 --> 00:41:58,349
we can plan it out.

946
00:41:58,432 --> 00:42:00,518
-We can match the dates.
-Let's talk about it.

947
00:42:00,601 --> 00:42:04,522
We could put all the Black Heart Chips
to the person who seems most popular.

948
00:42:05,105 --> 00:42:06,273
We can become king.

949
00:42:06,357 --> 00:42:08,651
Let's make one of us four the king.

950
00:42:08,734 --> 00:42:10,819
If one wants to go on a date
under this system,

951
00:42:10,903 --> 00:42:13,572
I felt like we needed the power of a king.

952
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:15,491
The one who gets the most Heart Chips

953
00:42:15,616 --> 00:42:17,576
and the fewest Black Heart Chips
becomes the king among us.

954
00:42:17,660 --> 00:42:19,703
Then, who should we pick?

955
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:23,499
And how many should we give
to secure their position?

956
00:42:23,582 --> 00:42:27,086
Wait, so three of us have to concentrate
our support to one person.

957
00:42:27,169 --> 00:42:28,212
If we put at least 100…

958
00:42:28,295 --> 00:42:29,880
Can we give it to the same sex?

959
00:42:29,964 --> 00:42:32,675
You can use the Black Heart Chips
to attack the same sex,

960
00:42:32,758 --> 00:42:34,802
-but I can't give any hearts to Jung-min.
-Right.

961
00:42:34,885 --> 00:42:36,345
You can only put in the women's boxes.

962
00:42:36,428 --> 00:42:37,888
Either you two pool them, or we do.

963
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:39,807
No, you can give it to the same sex.

964
00:42:39,890 --> 00:42:41,016
How can I give hearts to…

965
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:42,601
Why would I give Jung-min hearts?

966
00:42:45,563 --> 00:42:48,941
Honestly, I had a hard time understanding.

967
00:42:49,024 --> 00:42:50,109
I didn't get it.

968
00:42:50,192 --> 00:42:52,945
My brain was just not working.

969
00:42:53,028 --> 00:42:54,655
If we want to strategize,

970
00:42:54,738 --> 00:42:56,615
we have to speak up
about who we want to date.

971
00:42:56,699 --> 00:42:57,616
Right.

972
00:42:57,700 --> 00:42:59,118
Talk about who we want to date?

973
00:42:59,201 --> 00:43:01,287
-After you become king.
-Yeah, after you become king.

974
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:03,664
We have to get together
after we become king.

975
00:43:03,747 --> 00:43:05,124
We'll make one of us king

976
00:43:05,207 --> 00:43:09,878
and each person can meet the king
and tell them what we want.

977
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:12,256
-Go to the king's quarters and…
-The king's quarters?

978
00:43:12,339 --> 00:43:15,092
-How many Heart Chips do you have?
-I guess I have 250 Heart Chips.

979
00:43:15,175 --> 00:43:16,427
I haven't used any.

980
00:43:16,510 --> 00:43:17,344
Me…

981
00:43:17,970 --> 00:43:18,887
I have quite a lot.

982
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:20,514
So…

983
00:43:21,515 --> 00:43:23,350
You have the most, don't you?

984
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:25,436
You didn't vote yet.

985
00:43:25,519 --> 00:43:28,606
Ha-yoon has the most chips

986
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:31,400
and I actually have the most chips too.

987
00:43:31,483 --> 00:43:34,612
I didn't think I should tell them
the fact that I didn't vote.

988
00:43:34,695 --> 00:43:37,448
I have the advantage too, right?

989
00:43:37,531 --> 00:43:40,284
<i>I thought it would be easy</i>
<i>to make someone king.</i>

990
00:43:40,868 --> 00:43:42,077
You know what's insane?

991
00:43:42,161 --> 00:43:43,787
All the men have 200…

992
00:43:43,871 --> 00:43:45,581
-250 chips.
-250 chips.

993
00:43:45,664 --> 00:43:46,749
-250 chips.
-Yeah.

994
00:43:46,832 --> 00:43:48,667
249 chips and 248 chips.

995
00:43:48,751 --> 00:43:50,169
-Right.
-That's crazy.

996
00:43:50,252 --> 00:43:52,004
All of them have a lot of hearts.

997
00:43:52,588 --> 00:43:54,048
We have to figure out…

998
00:43:54,131 --> 00:43:56,175
But if they went on a date today,

999
00:43:56,258 --> 00:43:57,843
they have to give each other hearts.

1000
00:43:57,926 --> 00:44:02,014
Unless they loved their date so much
that they put in 200 hearts…

1001
00:44:02,097 --> 00:44:03,599
No one would do that.

1002
00:44:03,682 --> 00:44:06,185
-They may not even get 100.
-Right.

1003
00:44:06,268 --> 00:44:07,728
-I think I can give 100.
-It's slim.

1004
00:44:07,811 --> 00:44:09,146
Based on today's date?

1005
00:44:09,229 --> 00:44:12,066
Let's say we have 200 hearts.
We only have three nights left.

1006
00:44:12,149 --> 00:44:15,027
As you said,
we could use 100 to 200 hearts,

1007
00:44:15,110 --> 00:44:18,614
but it would become too costly
for us to choose someone to be king.

1008
00:44:18,697 --> 00:44:20,199
So I think,

1009
00:44:20,282 --> 00:44:23,661
since the average of 250
in four days is 65,

1010
00:44:23,744 --> 00:44:26,538
we can use that to give
someone 130 hearts.

1011
00:44:26,622 --> 00:44:30,209
Then, all of us can use each of
our Black Heart Chips to each person.

1012
00:44:30,292 --> 00:44:32,503
We'd be safe,
but we're in trouble if it goes over that.

1013
00:44:32,586 --> 00:44:35,255
-Then, we'll end up with nothing.
-Right.

1014
00:44:35,339 --> 00:44:36,924
-Then, we will…
-And…

1015
00:44:37,007 --> 00:44:37,841
We'll fall from grace.

1016
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:39,218
65 chips each isn't a bad idea.

1017
00:44:39,301 --> 00:44:41,303
-65 chips each is good.
-It adds up to 130.

1018
00:44:41,387 --> 00:44:43,013
It's more than half of 250 chips.

1019
00:44:43,097 --> 00:44:44,598
-They wouldn't give 130.
-Exactly.

1020
00:44:44,682 --> 00:44:45,683
Of course not.

1021
00:44:45,766 --> 00:44:47,643
If they give it, it's 200.
If not, it's 100.

1022
00:44:48,227 --> 00:44:49,978
-We wouldn't get 130.
-I'm wondering.

1023
00:44:50,062 --> 00:44:51,814
Of the 250 hearts

1024
00:44:51,897 --> 00:44:55,818
we can turn them into Black Heart Chips

1025
00:44:55,901 --> 00:44:59,571
and keep giving them out one
by one today, tomorrow, and the day after.

1026
00:44:59,655 --> 00:45:02,032
Then, all I need to spend is 50 hearts.

1027
00:45:02,116 --> 00:45:04,743
-Even with 50, I can confess my feelings.
-That's the issue.

1028
00:45:04,827 --> 00:45:05,869
But you see,

1029
00:45:05,953 --> 00:45:08,414
why would you make
more Black Heart Chips to do that?

1030
00:45:08,497 --> 00:45:11,417
I thought I could stop someone
from becoming king.

1031
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:13,168
Can you target that exact person?

1032
00:45:13,252 --> 00:45:15,379
-But I can…
-What if they could reject Black Hearts.

1033
00:45:15,462 --> 00:45:16,296
You might be right.

1034
00:45:16,380 --> 00:45:18,298
-At this rate--
-Rather than pulling down many,

1035
00:45:18,382 --> 00:45:20,717
it's more effective
to choose someone to be king, right?

1036
00:45:20,801 --> 00:45:23,846
It'd be hard to target a specific person,
but we can pick the best.

1037
00:45:23,929 --> 00:45:25,681
We're betting on that.

1038
00:45:25,764 --> 00:45:28,934
If we put in 65 hearts,
one of us can become king.

1039
00:45:30,102 --> 00:45:32,980
Is there anyone you want to
show your interest in today?

1040
00:45:33,063 --> 00:45:35,649
SILENCE

1041
00:45:36,275 --> 00:45:37,568
This is kind of hard to say.

1042
00:45:38,152 --> 00:45:39,319
What were you going to say?

1043
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:41,155
-W-w-what were you asking?
-Honestly…

1044
00:45:41,238 --> 00:45:42,739
-How do we answer that?
-Why'd you ask?

1045
00:45:42,823 --> 00:45:46,034
You may have certain moments
that you cherish.

1046
00:45:46,660 --> 00:45:49,246
Since today's vote is too calculating…

1047
00:45:49,329 --> 00:45:51,915
-But there's no point in saying it.
-It's okay, you can tell me.

1048
00:45:51,999 --> 00:45:54,585
Once you use up our hearts,
you can show your feelings anyway.

1049
00:45:54,668 --> 00:45:56,420
So not today?

1050
00:45:56,503 --> 00:45:58,589
Ha-yoon came up with the solution,

1051
00:45:58,672 --> 00:46:00,966
and we all teamed up

1052
00:46:01,049 --> 00:46:03,218
for a little scheming.

1053
00:46:03,302 --> 00:46:07,264
It could be that
we promised to give each other 65 hearts.

1054
00:46:07,347 --> 00:46:11,143
But what if someone changes their mind
and decides to give it to another?

1055
00:46:11,226 --> 00:46:13,645
At least, I won't…

1056
00:46:14,229 --> 00:46:16,023
I'd cut ties with them.

1057
00:46:16,106 --> 00:46:18,442
Today… That really put me off.

1058
00:46:19,234 --> 00:46:21,361
Gosh, it really does.

1059
00:46:21,445 --> 00:46:23,155
Let's not betray each other today.

1060
00:46:23,238 --> 00:46:24,406
Let's put our fists together.

1061
00:46:24,490 --> 00:46:25,491
Not today.

1062
00:46:25,574 --> 00:46:26,575
-Be honest.
-At least for today.

1063
00:46:26,658 --> 00:46:27,618
No betrayals.

1064
00:46:27,701 --> 00:46:30,287
-We can turn evil tomorrow.
-Right.

1065
00:46:30,370 --> 00:46:33,081
-You just have to say, "Your Highness."
-What if the king goes mad?

1066
00:46:33,707 --> 00:46:36,001
None of us here are crazy, right?

1067
00:46:36,084 --> 00:46:38,045
Not me. At least, not me.

1068
00:46:38,128 --> 00:46:40,047
Let's not work with these two.

1069
00:46:41,423 --> 00:46:42,716
They're so scary.

1070
00:46:42,799 --> 00:46:44,301
We need four to make a king.

1071
00:46:44,384 --> 00:46:45,427
They're scary.

1072
00:46:45,511 --> 00:46:47,888
-In the end--
-I want to go out with Ga-yeon tomorrow.

1073
00:46:50,349 --> 00:46:51,600
I'll keep this alliance.

1074
00:46:53,143 --> 00:46:54,228
Even if I become king,

1075
00:46:54,311 --> 00:46:56,772
I won't think about causing any chaos.

1076
00:46:56,855 --> 00:46:58,398
I'm okay with not being the king.

1077
00:47:00,776 --> 00:47:02,486
Let's write a contract instead.

1078
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:05,656
Get an ink pad.

1079
00:47:05,739 --> 00:47:08,617
-I mean it. Put lipstick on it.
-No, get a red ink pad.

1080
00:47:08,700 --> 00:47:10,410
Let's write it. Come on.

1081
00:47:10,494 --> 00:47:11,537
No reason not to.

1082
00:47:11,620 --> 00:47:13,038
Also,

1083
00:47:13,121 --> 00:47:14,498
why are you smiling so slyly?

1084
00:47:15,916 --> 00:47:16,875
What should I write?

1085
00:47:17,459 --> 00:47:18,961
Trust

1086
00:47:19,044 --> 00:47:20,003
and love one another.

1087
00:47:20,087 --> 00:47:21,129
"Trust and love one another."

1088
00:47:21,213 --> 00:47:22,047
Great words.

1089
00:47:22,130 --> 00:47:24,716
I don't think they'd know what it is
if we leave it like this.

1090
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:26,593
But also,

1091
00:47:26,677 --> 00:47:29,179
-what if the four check--
-Check us?

1092
00:47:29,263 --> 00:47:30,931
You're back.

1093
00:47:31,014 --> 00:47:32,140
Hello.

1094
00:47:32,224 --> 00:47:33,600
Black Heart Chips…

1095
00:47:33,684 --> 00:47:35,060
What's that?

1096
00:47:35,143 --> 00:47:36,520
HIDING IT

1097
00:47:36,603 --> 00:47:38,981
They must have gotten groceries.

1098
00:47:39,064 --> 00:47:39,898
Really?

1099
00:47:39,982 --> 00:47:41,525
-No way!
-Wow!

1100
00:47:41,608 --> 00:47:42,609
You're the best!

1101
00:47:42,693 --> 00:47:43,610
Thank you.

1102
00:47:43,694 --> 00:47:44,820
-You got groceries?
-Thank you.

1103
00:47:44,903 --> 00:47:46,238
-You got groceries?
-Yes.

1104
00:47:46,822 --> 00:47:48,198
-Wow.
-It looks good.

1105
00:47:48,282 --> 00:47:50,033
-Did you have fun?
-Yes.

1106
00:47:51,702 --> 00:47:52,953
They got groceries.

1107
00:47:53,036 --> 00:47:55,163
You look a lot happier.

1108
00:47:56,915 --> 00:47:58,584
Jung-min can't read the room.

1109
00:47:58,667 --> 00:48:00,711
What made him think they looked happier?

1110
00:48:00,794 --> 00:48:01,628
Did you have fun?

1111
00:48:01,712 --> 00:48:03,338
We should take this to the lounge.

1112
00:48:03,839 --> 00:48:06,049
We didn't know what to get so…

1113
00:48:06,633 --> 00:48:07,551
You even got meat.

1114
00:48:08,468 --> 00:48:09,469
Awesome!

1115
00:48:13,932 --> 00:48:15,392
You went straight for the chocolate.

1116
00:48:16,310 --> 00:48:17,311
Were you craving it?

1117
00:48:18,061 --> 00:48:21,148
He remembered that you wanted chocolate
and got you some.

1118
00:48:21,648 --> 00:48:23,609
Don't you think so? He only got chocolate.

1119
00:48:23,692 --> 00:48:25,152
There wasn't anything sweet here.

1120
00:48:25,235 --> 00:48:27,863
Why would he tell her that?

1121
00:48:27,946 --> 00:48:30,282
How is that going to help him?

1122
00:48:30,365 --> 00:48:31,825
The rest can go to the lounge.

1123
00:48:31,908 --> 00:48:33,869
I'll make us delicious <i>doenjang</i> stew.

1124
00:48:33,952 --> 00:48:35,579
We haven't had dinner yet.

1125
00:48:35,662 --> 00:48:37,039
-Really?
-Really?

1126
00:48:37,122 --> 00:48:38,123
We haven't eaten.

1127
00:48:38,206 --> 00:48:39,750
You haven't had dinner?

1128
00:48:39,833 --> 00:48:41,335
-We ate.
-We ate.

1129
00:48:41,418 --> 00:48:42,711
We had spicy blue crab soup,

1130
00:48:42,794 --> 00:48:43,754
soy sauce marinated crab,

1131
00:48:43,837 --> 00:48:45,547
-and spicy marinated crab.
-Yum!

1132
00:48:45,631 --> 00:48:48,759
I'm so jealous
you got to have my favorite dish.

1133
00:48:49,968 --> 00:48:51,595
I'm hungry.

1134
00:48:54,097 --> 00:48:55,724
Have some snacks.

1135
00:48:57,225 --> 00:48:58,101
So…

1136
00:49:00,646 --> 00:49:02,105
-What?
-We should decide.

1137
00:49:02,189 --> 00:49:03,565
Hasn't it been decided?

1138
00:49:03,649 --> 00:49:04,733
Who?

1139
00:49:04,816 --> 00:49:06,652
I think we can do that while we eat.

1140
00:49:06,735 --> 00:49:08,528
-It isn't that important.
-But they can hear us.

1141
00:49:08,612 --> 00:49:10,989
They'll come with us, won't they?

1142
00:49:11,073 --> 00:49:13,867
-But it doesn't matter who does it.
-Why not?

1143
00:49:14,034 --> 00:49:15,869
-That really doesn't matter.

1144
00:49:15,952 --> 00:49:16,787
Why not?

1145
00:49:16,870 --> 00:49:18,997
Because the king has to
do what the other three says.

1146
00:49:19,081 --> 00:49:21,249
But shouldn't we decide among ourselves?

1147
00:49:21,333 --> 00:49:22,626
Of course, we have to decide.

1148
00:49:22,709 --> 00:49:24,086
We have a lot of time though.

1149
00:49:24,169 --> 00:49:25,295
-Okay.
-First,

1150
00:49:25,379 --> 00:49:27,297
-the contract.
-But we might not… Right.

1151
00:49:27,381 --> 00:49:30,509
I won't do it
if we don't sign the contract.

1152
00:49:30,592 --> 00:49:32,719
Me neither. Those guys are scary.

1153
00:49:33,553 --> 00:49:37,015
Shouldn't we write the contract
and decide who'll become king?

1154
00:49:37,099 --> 00:49:38,433
-Before they come.
-It's okay.

1155
00:49:38,517 --> 00:49:39,893
Why do you say it's okay?

1156
00:49:39,976 --> 00:49:41,812
-We can take our time.
-Really?

1157
00:49:41,895 --> 00:49:43,271
I don't think we have a lot of time.

1158
00:49:43,355 --> 00:49:44,231
Who wants to do it?

1159
00:49:44,314 --> 00:49:45,774
Should we give you 65 hearts each?

1160
00:49:45,857 --> 00:49:47,150
We'll concentrate our votes.

1161
00:49:47,234 --> 00:49:48,694
-Then…
-Hurry.

1162
00:49:48,777 --> 00:49:49,653
-One of you two.
-One of you two.

1163
00:49:49,736 --> 00:49:51,446
-One of you two.
-It doesn't matter.

1164
00:49:51,530 --> 00:49:53,031
What should we do? Should I do it?

1165
00:49:53,115 --> 00:49:54,658
-Hye-won can do it.
-Okay, Hye-won.

1166
00:49:54,741 --> 00:49:57,911
If I become king I might…

1167
00:49:57,994 --> 00:50:00,330
-You'll get all these other ideas.
-Yeah.

1168
00:50:00,831 --> 00:50:03,166
First of all, Ha-yoon has a lot of chips

1169
00:50:03,250 --> 00:50:05,752
and I have a lot of chips,
but no one else knows that.

1170
00:50:05,836 --> 00:50:07,087
So maybe the men should give the votes.

1171
00:50:07,796 --> 00:50:10,424
Even if Ga-yeon isn't the king,

1172
00:50:10,507 --> 00:50:14,136
I thought Hye-won would
match Ga-yeon with me.

1173
00:50:14,219 --> 00:50:16,179
And I could sense Ga-yeon's feelings

1174
00:50:16,263 --> 00:50:17,597
about me a little bit.

1175
00:50:17,681 --> 00:50:19,182
Besides the time the four of us spent,

1176
00:50:19,266 --> 00:50:21,184
the two of us spent
a lot of time together,

1177
00:50:21,268 --> 00:50:23,729
so I felt pretty sure about it.

1178
00:50:23,812 --> 00:50:27,441
Honestly, I didn't want to become king.

1179
00:50:28,525 --> 00:50:29,943
I keep making eye contact with Kyung-ho.

1180
00:50:30,026 --> 00:50:33,655
They'd last a long time
and it happened frequently.

1181
00:50:33,739 --> 00:50:35,741
I don't know if I'm attracted to him

1182
00:50:35,824 --> 00:50:39,035
or he just draws attention.

1183
00:50:40,036 --> 00:50:40,871
I was curious.

1184
00:50:40,954 --> 00:50:43,290
But if I became king

1185
00:50:43,373 --> 00:50:45,208
and went on a date with Jung-min,

1186
00:50:45,292 --> 00:50:48,128
I was worried it would end up
like I was picking a lane,

1187
00:50:48,211 --> 00:50:51,214
so I just wanted to leave it to fate.

1188
00:50:54,843 --> 00:50:55,886
Where did everyone go?

1189
00:50:55,969 --> 00:50:57,596
They went to the lounge. Want to go?

1190
00:50:58,096 --> 00:50:59,014
Yeah, we should go.

1191
00:50:59,097 --> 00:51:00,557
Why did they go to the lounge?

1192
00:51:00,640 --> 00:51:01,892
I think they went to cook.

1193
00:51:01,975 --> 00:51:03,059
Really? Let's go.

1194
00:51:03,143 --> 00:51:05,103
No, go ahead. I'll be there soon.

1195
00:51:05,937 --> 00:51:06,897
You want to wait for me?

1196
00:51:07,898 --> 00:51:08,899
I'll wait.

1197
00:51:08,982 --> 00:51:10,108
Come inside and wait.

1198
00:51:20,786 --> 00:51:23,330
<i>I had a really hard time.</i>

1199
00:51:23,413 --> 00:51:25,207
It felt kind of awkward too.

1200
00:51:25,874 --> 00:51:27,626
Because I looked so down,

1201
00:51:28,376 --> 00:51:32,005
I could tell that he was
trying to look after me,

1202
00:51:32,088 --> 00:51:34,424
but perhaps it's because he felt sorry.

1203
00:51:36,259 --> 00:51:38,595
Wait, let's each make a promise.

1204
00:51:38,678 --> 00:51:40,305
-Promise already.
-Yeah.

1205
00:51:40,388 --> 00:51:41,765
Do you have a pen?

1206
00:51:41,848 --> 00:51:43,058
-Give it to me.
-A pen?

1207
00:51:43,141 --> 00:51:44,893
You won't betray us if you become king?

1208
00:51:44,976 --> 00:51:46,520
Do I look like I would?

1209
00:51:46,603 --> 00:51:48,897
I won't do it until we sign the contract.

1210
00:51:49,856 --> 00:51:51,691
-You said you liked me.
-I will…

1211
00:51:51,775 --> 00:51:53,485
-I'll get it.
-We'll write a contract--

1212
00:51:53,568 --> 00:51:55,403
-Ga-yeon doesn't trust me.
-I can hear everything.

1213
00:51:55,487 --> 00:51:56,905
That's why we're writing a contract.

1214
00:51:57,489 --> 00:51:58,365
Did you get the pen?

1215
00:51:58,448 --> 00:51:59,825
Let's do it over there.

1216
00:51:59,908 --> 00:52:01,159
One person at a time.

1217
00:52:01,243 --> 00:52:02,577
Leave it here.

1218
00:52:03,537 --> 00:52:05,956
When you sign the contract,
print your name, then sign it.

1219
00:52:06,039 --> 00:52:06,873
Okay.

1220
00:52:12,921 --> 00:52:15,006
Isn't it our first time in the lounge?

1221
00:52:18,510 --> 00:52:20,053
The two are coming.

1222
00:52:21,930 --> 00:52:23,139
I'll get some soju.

1223
00:52:23,640 --> 00:52:25,350
Should we cook the meat in here?

1224
00:52:25,433 --> 00:52:26,726
Can you cook it in that?

1225
00:52:27,310 --> 00:52:28,687
I'm worried they'll stick.

1226
00:52:28,770 --> 00:52:29,771
We can coat it with oil.

1227
00:52:33,859 --> 00:52:35,277
<i>I put the contract</i>

1228
00:52:35,360 --> 00:52:37,654
<i>in a notebook next to the drawings</i>

1229
00:52:37,737 --> 00:52:39,447
<i>that were on display.</i>

1230
00:52:40,949 --> 00:52:42,659
<i>I hid it right under their noses.</i>

1231
00:52:44,786 --> 00:52:47,622
DO-GEON AND CHAE-RIN ARE BACK

1232
00:52:48,331 --> 00:52:49,749
It must've been so fun!

1233
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:50,667
How cool.

1234
00:52:50,750 --> 00:52:51,960
-I'm jealous.
-What's that?

1235
00:52:52,043 --> 00:52:52,878
It must've been fun.

1236
00:52:52,961 --> 00:52:54,629
You went on a drive in that car?

1237
00:52:54,713 --> 00:52:55,672
-Yeah.
-Wow.

1238
00:52:56,381 --> 00:52:57,799
-How nice.
-What were you doing?

1239
00:52:57,883 --> 00:52:59,676
-We were cooking.
-Really?

1240
00:53:00,427 --> 00:53:03,054
You guys looked cool
when you got out of that car.

1241
00:53:03,138 --> 00:53:04,306
I'm jealous.

1242
00:53:04,890 --> 00:53:06,975
-Didn't we have fun?
-Didn't we have fun?

1243
00:53:09,603 --> 00:53:10,604
I thought no younger men.

1244
00:53:10,687 --> 00:53:12,689
This is too much. I'm getting so excited.

1245
00:53:13,273 --> 00:53:15,317
-Didn't we have fun?
-Didn't we have fun?

1246
00:53:18,194 --> 00:53:19,362
I hear it sizzling.

1247
00:53:20,989 --> 00:53:22,741
It's going to be delicious.

1248
00:53:23,408 --> 00:53:24,618
-What a waste, right?
-Yeah.

1249
00:53:25,744 --> 00:53:27,537
I don't know if I did it right.

1250
00:53:27,621 --> 00:53:28,997
You're cooking the meat okay?

1251
00:53:29,706 --> 00:53:30,749
Aren't I doing a good job?

1252
00:53:30,832 --> 00:53:31,875
Did you salt it?

1253
00:53:32,918 --> 00:53:34,085
No.

1254
00:53:34,169 --> 00:53:35,378
Are you doing it right?

1255
00:53:35,462 --> 00:53:37,047
-I'll sprinkle some on.
-Okay.

1256
00:53:39,049 --> 00:53:40,884
I'm not good at grilling meat,

1257
00:53:40,967 --> 00:53:43,178
but I wanted to act like I was good at it.

1258
00:53:43,261 --> 00:53:44,721
I wanted to mess with her.

1259
00:53:44,804 --> 00:53:47,265
I told her to sprinkle some salt
since she didn't.

1260
00:53:47,349 --> 00:53:49,059
Then, I told her to sprinkle some pepper.

1261
00:53:49,142 --> 00:53:51,645
I started it off
with light conversation like that

1262
00:53:51,728 --> 00:53:54,898
and tried to grill the meat together.

1263
00:53:55,398 --> 00:53:56,316
I need scissors.

1264
00:54:01,446 --> 00:54:03,573
Shouldn't you use these to grill the meat?

1265
00:54:05,575 --> 00:54:06,409
Right?

1266
00:54:06,493 --> 00:54:08,161
What are you doing?

1267
