01:14:48,734 --> 01:14:50,694
I'm not sure what's going on.

1742
01:14:53,322 --> 01:14:54,823
-Maybe I'm wrong.
-What's up?

1743
01:14:54,907 --> 01:14:56,492
-What is it?
-This is my assumption.

1744
01:14:57,117 --> 01:14:59,036
While we were gone,

1745
01:14:59,119 --> 01:15:00,787
the four were left behind, right?

1746
01:15:00,871 --> 01:15:01,830
I think

1747
01:15:03,040 --> 01:15:04,750
they're going to make one of them king.

1748
01:15:06,126 --> 01:15:09,838
So what you're saying is
besides the ones that went on a date,

1749
01:15:09,922 --> 01:15:13,133
the four that were left
are going to make one of themselves king?

1750
01:15:13,717 --> 01:15:15,219
Do you want to be king?

1751
01:15:15,302 --> 01:15:17,387
King? It would be nice.

1752
01:15:20,182 --> 01:15:21,058
Me too.

1753
01:15:21,141 --> 01:15:22,351
Want me to invest in you?

1754
01:15:24,811 --> 01:15:27,564
If the tables turn because of this… Man.

1755
01:15:27,648 --> 01:15:28,857
Want me to invest in you?

1756
01:15:30,567 --> 01:15:32,152
-To shock them?
-Yeah.

1757
01:15:32,236 --> 01:15:33,111
Then,

1758
01:15:33,820 --> 01:15:37,741
how much do we have to spend
to become king?

1759
01:15:38,367 --> 01:15:40,118
-I'll just pour it in.
-Pour it in?

1760
01:15:41,662 --> 01:15:42,871
By the way…

1761
01:15:42,955 --> 01:15:45,707
-She was looking for you.
-Chae-rin was looking for you.

1762
01:15:46,291 --> 01:15:47,960
She looked speechless.

1763
01:15:50,629 --> 01:15:51,588
For real?

1764
01:15:51,672 --> 01:15:54,132
-Where did she go?
-She went to talk with Do-geon.

1765
01:15:58,512 --> 01:16:00,806
MOON CHAE-RIN
ENTERS THE HEART ROOM

1766
01:16:03,100 --> 01:16:04,226
What's this?

1767
01:16:06,770 --> 01:16:08,981
"The other person's number
of Heart Chips…"

1768
01:16:09,565 --> 01:16:11,608
That was insane. Truly.

1769
01:16:13,026 --> 01:16:16,530
<i>There was something</i>
<i>I never expected at all.</i>

1770
01:16:17,114 --> 01:16:18,699
Gosh. Hang on.

1771
01:16:21,118 --> 01:16:24,621
Everyone except those four just found out
that the Black Heart Chips exist.

1772
01:16:25,289 --> 01:16:26,873
<i>How am I supposed to use these?</i>

1773
01:16:26,957 --> 01:16:28,834
<i>Who should I use them on?</i>

1774
01:16:30,168 --> 01:16:32,129
<i>I thought about it a lot.</i>

1775
01:16:34,840 --> 01:16:36,675
CHAE-RIN: 10 BLACK HEARTS → ??

1776
01:16:37,551 --> 01:16:39,428
<i>And to Do-geon,</i>

1777
01:16:40,512 --> 01:16:42,723
<i>I gave him 20 Heart Chips.</i>

1778
01:16:47,019 --> 01:16:49,479
CHAE-RIN'S VOTE
20 → DO-GEON, 10 BLACK HEARTS → ??

1779
01:16:50,814 --> 01:16:53,108
PARK DO-GEON
ENTERS THE HEART ROOM

1780
01:16:53,942 --> 01:16:56,570
<i>When I read what was written on the note,</i>

1781
01:16:56,653 --> 01:17:01,116
<i>I realized that the Black Heart Chips</i>
<i>can be used effectively</i>

1782
01:17:01,700 --> 01:17:04,786
<i>if people were to form an alliance</i>
to make someone king.

1783
01:17:05,537 --> 01:17:10,542
<i>And I thought Jung-min</i>
<i>could end up being king this time.</i>

1784
01:17:11,793 --> 01:17:13,587
DO-GEON: 10 BLACK HEARTS → JUNG-MIN

1785
01:17:15,297 --> 01:17:19,301
<i>I only put two hearts</i>
<i>in </i><i>Chae-rin's </i><i>box </i><i>yesterday,</i>

1786
01:17:19,843 --> 01:17:22,804
<i>but my feelings for her</i>
<i>have </i><i>grown </i><i>since </i><i>then so…</i>

1787
01:17:27,100 --> 01:17:29,936
THE RED HEART CHIPS INCREASED
AS MUCH AS HIS FEELINGS DID

1788
01:17:32,856 --> 01:17:35,651
<i>I wrote, "See you at Gireum Station."</i>

1789
01:17:35,734 --> 01:17:37,277
SEE YOU AT GIREUM STATION

1790
01:17:37,361 --> 01:17:38,528
I live near Korea University.

1791
01:17:39,154 --> 01:17:39,988
Anam?

1792
01:17:40,072 --> 01:17:42,032
-Where do you live?
-Near Gireum.

1793
01:17:42,115 --> 01:17:43,033
-Really?
-Yeah.

1794
01:17:43,116 --> 01:17:44,368
Why do we live so close?

1795
01:17:44,451 --> 01:17:46,453
That's only a 10-minute walk.

1796
01:17:47,871 --> 01:17:49,956
I wanted her to know it was me.

1797
01:17:50,040 --> 01:17:51,833
That's why I wrote that.

1798
01:17:52,793 --> 01:17:54,753
You draw really well.

1799
01:17:55,337 --> 01:17:56,505
That's insane.

1800
01:17:56,588 --> 01:17:59,174
Can you tell what it is?

1801
01:17:59,841 --> 01:18:01,009
It looks like a butterfly.

1802
01:18:01,551 --> 01:18:03,303
Yeah, make it pretty.

1803
01:18:03,387 --> 01:18:04,680
-Pretty?
-Yeah.

1804
01:18:06,181 --> 01:18:08,266
You guys look like you're in a web drama.

1805
01:18:08,350 --> 01:18:09,518
Yeah, the three of you.

1806
01:18:09,601 --> 01:18:12,354
One of us has to win him over.

1807
01:18:13,188 --> 01:18:14,064
We have to charm him?

1808
01:18:14,648 --> 01:18:17,943
I love how you all look.
Even your outfits go well together.

1809
01:18:18,026 --> 01:18:19,027
-Really?
-Yeah.

1810
01:18:19,111 --> 01:18:20,654
Should I dress cute or hot tomorrow?

1811
01:18:20,737 --> 01:18:22,531
-I pick hot.
-Go with hot.

1812
01:18:22,614 --> 01:18:24,658
Then I'm going to go all out tomorrow.

1813
01:18:24,741 --> 01:18:26,493
What are you going to wear tomorrow?

1814
01:18:26,576 --> 01:18:27,619
Tomorrow?

1815
01:18:28,453 --> 01:18:30,122
Something mature.

1816
01:18:30,956 --> 01:18:32,165
-Geez.
-Gosh!

1817
01:18:33,458 --> 01:18:35,335
If you're 22 years old, you're an adult!

1818
01:18:35,419 --> 01:18:38,547
Kyung-ho, I get what you're saying.

1819
01:18:38,630 --> 01:18:39,798
I get it.

1820
01:18:39,881 --> 01:18:41,883
But I feel so bad for Ye-rim.

1821
01:18:41,967 --> 01:18:43,677
She wants to wear something mature.

1822
01:18:43,760 --> 01:18:45,554
He keeps talking to her
because she's on his mind.

1823
01:18:45,637 --> 01:18:46,596
Exactly.

1824
01:18:46,680 --> 01:18:49,141
If you're 22 years old,
you're definitely an adult!

1825
01:18:49,224 --> 01:18:52,352
If you can buy cigarettes and alcohol
at a convenience store, you're an adult.

1826
01:18:53,603 --> 01:18:54,521
Something mature.

1827
01:18:54,604 --> 01:18:55,439
Mature?

1828
01:18:56,064 --> 01:18:57,023
No.

1829
01:18:57,858 --> 01:18:58,775
Never mind.

1830
01:19:03,029 --> 01:19:07,451
<i>I didn't want to be king.</i>
<i>I just wanted to do what I was told.</i>

1831
01:19:08,118 --> 01:19:09,494
Even if I became king,

1832
01:19:09,578 --> 01:19:11,955
I wouldn't want to burden him
so I wouldn't choose him.

1833
01:19:13,039 --> 01:19:16,334
<i>But no one would choose me</i>
<i>besides Kyung-ho.</i>

1834
01:19:17,586 --> 01:19:19,004
<i>I really wanted to be king.</i>

1835
01:19:19,713 --> 01:19:20,589
I was

1836
01:19:21,590 --> 01:19:22,591
so confused.

1837
01:19:23,175 --> 01:19:27,053
I wanted to create an environment
where I can gather my thoughts.

1838
01:19:28,138 --> 01:19:30,515
KANG KYUNG-HO
ENTERS THE HEART ROOM

1839
01:19:33,101 --> 01:19:35,020
<i>But there was something unfamiliar there.</i>

1840
01:19:39,399 --> 01:19:41,943
<i>I found out that</i>
<i>the </i><i>Black Heart Chips were negative chips.</i>

1841
01:19:42,819 --> 01:19:45,155
LEE YE-RIM
ENTERS THE HEART ROOM

1842
01:19:47,157 --> 01:19:49,242
<i>I thought it was so mean.</i>

1843
01:19:49,326 --> 01:19:53,455
Heart Chips are meant to be used
to express how they feel.

1844
01:19:53,538 --> 01:19:56,500
<i>But if someone else deducts that,</i>

1845
01:19:56,583 --> 01:19:58,877
<i>it could cause a huge misunderstanding.</i>

1846
01:19:58,960 --> 01:20:00,921
<i>So I didn't put any in.</i>

1847
01:20:09,888 --> 01:20:13,099
<i>If I could only vote for one person,</i>

1848
01:20:14,184 --> 01:20:16,895
<i>I would have had to think</i>
<i>even more about it.</i>

1849
01:20:17,896 --> 01:20:20,690
<i>I went on a date with Ye-rim</i>
<i>and I had a great time,</i>

1850
01:20:21,483 --> 01:20:24,027
<i>but I keep getting more curious</i>
<i>about Ga-yeon.</i>

1851
01:20:24,110 --> 01:20:26,404
Is it different when you meet outside?

1852
01:20:26,488 --> 01:20:28,365
-You want to go out?
-Yeah.

1853
01:20:28,949 --> 01:20:31,034
So when I heard I can cast multiple votes,

1854
01:20:31,117 --> 01:20:32,202
I felt at ease.

1855
01:20:34,371 --> 01:20:36,665
?? → GA-YEON, ?? → YE-RIM,
?? BLACK HEARTS → ??

1856
01:20:40,210 --> 01:20:42,921
<i>Honestly,</i>
<i>I considered not voting for anyone.</i>

1857
01:20:43,922 --> 01:20:45,674
<i>But there's still a lot of time left,</i>

1858
01:20:45,757 --> 01:20:49,886
<i>so I thought I should get to know</i>
<i>someone else and talk to them more.</i>

1859
01:20:51,888 --> 01:20:54,474
I'D LIKE TO GET TO KNOW YOU

1860
01:20:55,225 --> 01:20:57,394
YE-RIM: 1 HEART → ??

1861
01:20:58,228 --> 01:21:02,524
<i>And I thought a lot about</i>
<i>whether </i><i>I should vote for Kyung-ho or not…</i>

1862
01:21:07,571 --> 01:21:10,657
<i>The Heart Chip vote</i>
<i>for the second day has ended.</i>

1863
01:21:11,741 --> 01:21:14,870
<i>Female participants,</i>
<i>please begin checking your vote boxes.</i>

1864
01:21:14,953 --> 01:21:18,623
<i>Open your box</i>
<i>and only check what's inside yours.</i>

1865
01:21:19,374 --> 01:21:21,167
I don't want to open it.

1866
01:21:31,845 --> 01:21:34,264
<i>When I opened it,</i>
<i>there was a message that said,</i>

1867
01:21:34,848 --> 01:21:35,849
<i>"See you at Gireum Station."</i>

1868
01:21:35,932 --> 01:21:38,435
DO-GEON → CHAE-RIN
45 HEARTS

1869
01:21:38,518 --> 01:21:40,103
Wow, he's so direct.

1870
01:21:40,687 --> 01:21:44,274
I got the impression that he wanted to
keep seeing me after we left here.

1871
01:21:44,357 --> 01:21:46,902
He's usually not very expressive,

1872
01:21:46,985 --> 01:21:50,614
but then he suddenly said something
that made my heart race.

1873
01:21:51,197 --> 01:21:54,034
I've never viewed younger guys as men.

1874
01:21:54,117 --> 01:21:55,619
I may be different.

1875
01:21:56,786 --> 01:21:59,122
Yeah, you may be different.

1876
01:21:59,205 --> 01:22:02,459
I liked it even more because
he didn't seem like the type to say that.

1877
01:22:02,542 --> 01:22:05,170
"Hey, he knows
how to say things like that?"

1878
01:22:06,963 --> 01:22:09,341
<i>But I had quite a lot</i>
<i>of Black Heart Chips.</i>

1879
01:22:09,841 --> 01:22:11,635
Who is intimidated by me?

1880
01:22:11,718 --> 01:22:12,928
It feels good.

1881
01:22:17,057 --> 01:22:20,810
<i>Or is someone interested in Do-geon?</i>

1882
01:22:21,394 --> 01:22:22,604
Did Ye-rim put them in?

1883
01:22:23,313 --> 01:22:26,816
To me, it seemed like
Ye-rim's second choice was Do-geon.

1884
01:22:27,400 --> 01:22:30,111
Can't you just be friends
with someone born in 2003?

1885
01:22:31,821 --> 01:22:32,864
Should we talk casually?

1886
01:22:32,948 --> 01:22:34,074
Feel free to.

1887
01:22:35,033 --> 01:22:36,743
-Are my dark circles really bad?
-What?

1888
01:22:36,826 --> 01:22:37,661
Are my dark circles bad?

1889
01:22:37,744 --> 01:22:38,870
-Me?
-Me.

1890
01:22:40,038 --> 01:22:41,206
I thought you meant me.

1891
01:22:41,289 --> 01:22:43,083
I wasn't asking you.

1892
01:22:43,166 --> 01:22:45,126
I have dark circles too.

1893
01:22:47,420 --> 01:22:49,714
That one vote that Ye-rim cast

1894
01:22:49,798 --> 01:22:51,883
-must be for Do-geon.
-It may be Do-geon.

1895
01:22:51,967 --> 01:22:53,343
I hope it works out.

1896
01:22:53,426 --> 01:22:55,637
-They look good together.
-They do.

1897
01:22:55,720 --> 01:22:56,638
They look good.

1898
01:22:59,432 --> 01:23:02,394
<i>Maybe she wanted to</i>
<i>go on her next date with Do-geon.</i>

1899
01:23:02,477 --> 01:23:04,396
<i>Maybe that's why she put them in mine.</i>

1900
01:23:05,146 --> 01:23:08,650
But when I think of Chae-rin, I feel bad.

1901
01:23:08,733 --> 01:23:10,360
It's okay. She'll meet someone else.

1902
01:23:19,494 --> 01:23:20,662
Kyung-ho…

1903
01:23:22,414 --> 01:23:24,374
wrote, "I had fun."

1904
01:23:26,167 --> 01:23:28,753
<i>It was the same color as the first day.</i>

1905
01:23:29,295 --> 01:23:33,508
<i>I think I was too petty and cautious</i>
<i>when I only put one in the first time.</i>

1906
01:23:36,803 --> 01:23:38,972
<i>My feelings for her grew that much.</i>

1907
01:23:42,058 --> 01:23:44,394
KYUNG-HO: 15 HEARTS → YE-RIM

1908
01:23:45,061 --> 01:23:47,313
<i>I was relieved.</i>

1909
01:23:47,939 --> 01:23:49,899
Perhaps I was being too negative.

1910
01:23:49,983 --> 01:23:52,235
I guess he hasn't completely let go of me.

1911
01:23:52,318 --> 01:23:53,361
That's what I thought.

1912
01:23:55,030 --> 01:23:58,283
<i>But I had quite</i>
<i>a lot of Black Heart Chips.</i>

1913
01:23:59,492 --> 01:24:01,369
<i>I think I had about 30 to 40.</i>

1914
01:24:01,453 --> 01:24:04,414
YE-RIM'S BOX
KYUNG-HO: 15, ??: 30 BLACK HEARTS

1915
01:24:04,998 --> 01:24:07,375
I think Kyung-ho put those in mine.

1916
01:24:09,169 --> 01:24:11,713
Maybe he thinks that
I'll choose him if I became king.

1917
01:24:12,630 --> 01:24:13,631
What?

1918
01:24:13,715 --> 01:24:16,426
Ye-rim, you got it completely wrong.

1919
01:24:16,926 --> 01:24:19,095
He didn't want me to become king,

1920
01:24:19,179 --> 01:24:21,806
so he put in the Black Heart Chips too.

1921
01:24:25,685 --> 01:24:27,979
<i>I put 10 Black Heart Chips on Ye-rim.</i>

1922
01:24:28,563 --> 01:24:33,777
You see,
I don't know exactly how Do-geon feels.

1923
01:24:34,360 --> 01:24:37,489
<i>I thought Do-geon's second choice</i>
<i>was Ye-rim,</i>

1924
01:24:37,572 --> 01:24:40,533
<i>and Ye-rim's second choice was Do-geon.</i>

1925
01:24:44,370 --> 01:24:46,498
CHAE-RIN: 10 BLACK HEARTS → YE-RIM

1926
01:24:50,585 --> 01:24:51,795
<i>When I opened mine,</i>

1927
01:24:52,462 --> 01:24:54,631
<i>I saw that I had a lot of hearts.</i>

1928
01:24:55,924 --> 01:24:58,051
<i>But there were some Black Heart Chips.</i>

1929
01:24:58,134 --> 01:24:59,594
Our plan was

1930
01:24:59,677 --> 01:25:01,846
to not put any Black Heart Chips
into each other's boxes.

1931
01:25:01,930 --> 01:25:03,598
Then why did I have Black Heart Chips?

1932
01:25:04,265 --> 01:25:08,978
<i>I was just captivated by</i>
<i>what was in my Heart Chip box.</i>

1933
01:25:12,941 --> 01:25:15,652
<i>I didn't get any on the first day.</i>

1934
01:25:17,570 --> 01:25:19,239
LEARN TO DANCE WELL, HONEYBEE
LET'S HAVE MORE FUN THAN ANYONE

1935
01:25:19,322 --> 01:25:20,406
<i>I had three.</i>

1936
01:25:21,157 --> 01:25:23,118
Wait, Ga-yeon may become king.

1937
01:25:23,201 --> 01:25:24,994
Everybody voted for her except one.

1938
01:25:25,078 --> 01:25:26,996
-The brown one is Kyung-ho, right?
-Yeah.

1939
01:25:27,080 --> 01:25:28,248
And the blue is Jung-min.

1940
01:25:28,331 --> 01:25:29,707
-Who's red?
-What about red?

1941
01:25:30,291 --> 01:25:33,336
<i>I didn't have any yesterday,</i>
<i>but I have a lot today. It felt good.</i>

1942
01:25:34,212 --> 01:25:36,673
<i>"We'll have more fun</i>
<i>than </i><i>anyone </i><i>else </i><i>tomorrow."</i>

1943
01:25:36,756 --> 01:25:38,216
Jung-min.

1944
01:25:38,299 --> 01:25:40,051
We were the ones that plotted,

1945
01:25:40,135 --> 01:25:42,053
so he knew we'd go on a date.

1946
01:25:42,929 --> 01:25:45,682
<i>That's why he wrote,</i>
<i>"We'll have more fun than anyone else."</i>

1947
01:25:46,224 --> 01:25:47,433
HONEYBEE

1948
01:25:47,517 --> 01:25:49,853
<i>"Honeybee" is from Kyung-ho.</i>

1949
01:25:49,936 --> 01:25:52,355
Kyung-ho and I were drawing

1950
01:25:52,438 --> 01:25:54,107
and I drew a honeybee.

1951
01:25:54,190 --> 01:25:56,609
I'll draw the eyes right here…

1952
01:25:57,569 --> 01:25:59,028
You can do the tail like this.

1953
01:25:59,112 --> 01:26:00,405
That's so cute.

1954
01:26:03,616 --> 01:26:06,161
KYUNG-HO: 14 HEARTS → GA-YEON

1955
01:26:07,412 --> 01:26:08,288
<i>And…</i>

1956
01:26:08,872 --> 01:26:10,081
<i>"Learn to dance well."</i>

1957
01:26:11,332 --> 01:26:13,751
I think it's Do-geon.

1958
01:26:13,835 --> 01:26:15,420
No, go like this.

1959
01:26:16,045 --> 01:26:17,422
Why can't I do that?

1960
01:26:18,006 --> 01:26:20,383
I can't do it. I can't grasp it.

1961
01:26:22,093 --> 01:26:23,303
Hey, you're good.

1962
01:26:23,386 --> 01:26:24,220
He's better than me.

1963
01:26:25,180 --> 01:26:26,139
I saw that.

1964
01:26:26,222 --> 01:26:28,057
-Good, right?
-You get a smiley sticker.

1965
01:26:29,350 --> 01:26:33,188
<i>I'd like to get to know Ga-yeon better.</i>

1966
01:26:34,105 --> 01:26:37,942
<i>I want to learn more about her</i>
<i>so I wrote her a note.</i>

1967
01:26:38,610 --> 01:26:40,361
DO-GEON'S VOTE
45 → CHAE-RIN, 5 → GA-YEON

1968
01:26:40,445 --> 01:26:41,571
10 BLACK HEARTS → JUNG-MIN

1969
01:26:41,654 --> 01:26:43,323
Do-geon, you traitor.

1970
01:26:43,406 --> 01:26:45,950
-What about Gireum Station?
-And "See you at Gireum Station?"

1971
01:26:46,576 --> 01:26:49,579
<i>I thought it would be nice</i>
<i>to chat with all of them.</i>

1972
01:26:50,872 --> 01:26:53,249
Because multiple votes were allowed,

1973
01:26:53,333 --> 01:26:55,543
I was their second choice.

1974
01:26:56,211 --> 01:26:57,212
GA-YEON'S BOX

1975
01:26:57,295 --> 01:26:59,631
JUNG-MIN: ??, KYUNG-HO: 14,
DO-GEON: 5, ??: 10

1976
01:26:59,714 --> 01:27:02,759
GA-YEON RECEIVED HEART CHIPS FROM 3 MEN

1977
01:27:02,842 --> 01:27:06,512
<i>The female contestants</i>
<i>have finished checking their boxes.</i>

1978
01:27:07,597 --> 01:27:10,058
You know what I just thought of?

1979
01:27:10,642 --> 01:27:12,518
Since we could cast multiple votes,

1980
01:27:12,602 --> 01:27:15,188
we can see the connections now.

1981
01:27:16,522 --> 01:27:17,607
Isn't that no fun?

1982
01:27:18,733 --> 01:27:22,987
To be honest,
haven't we all ranked the guys?

1983
01:27:23,071 --> 01:27:25,615
Some relationships may be solid,

1984
01:27:25,698 --> 01:27:27,575
but we could get to know…

1985
01:27:27,659 --> 01:27:30,161
-Get to know someone we haven't yet?
-Yeah.

1986
01:27:30,745 --> 01:27:32,080
She doesn't want to go out with Jung-min.

1987
01:27:32,163 --> 01:27:33,039
-Ga-yeon?
-Yeah.

1988
01:27:33,122 --> 01:27:36,084
If she goes on a date with him tomorrow,
it could make them an official couple.

1989
01:27:36,167 --> 01:27:38,670
She feels uncomfortable since
she wants to get to know the others too.

1990
01:27:38,753 --> 01:27:40,797
-That's why she said that.
-Yeah.

1991
01:27:40,880 --> 01:27:42,715
"Isn't that no fun?"
She was hinting at it.

1992
01:27:42,799 --> 01:27:44,259
-What's no fun? It's so fun.
-Yeah.

1993
01:27:44,342 --> 01:27:45,343
It's so fun for us.

1994
01:27:45,426 --> 01:27:47,762
-Hye-won is supposed to be king, right?
-Yeah.

1995
01:27:47,845 --> 01:27:49,514
She's dropping subtle hints to Hye-won.

1996
01:27:49,597 --> 01:27:52,558
"Even if you become king,
don't match me with Jung-min."

1997
01:27:53,142 --> 01:27:56,479
<i>Male participants,</i>
<i>please begin checking your vote boxes.</i>

1998
01:27:57,689 --> 01:27:59,607
It's so nerve-racking, isn't it?

1999
01:28:04,279 --> 01:28:05,280
The alphabet T?

2000
01:28:06,656 --> 01:28:08,116
<i>I was a bit caught off guard.</i>

2001
01:28:12,787 --> 01:28:15,957
<i>I wrote "T" on the note.</i>

2002
01:28:16,541 --> 01:28:18,084
Because I love peppermint tea…

2003
01:28:18,668 --> 01:28:20,795
Think of me when you see peppermint tea.

2004
01:28:20,878 --> 01:28:22,839
How do I get peppermint tea?

2005
01:28:23,339 --> 01:28:27,218
<i>It was fun to see him trying</i>
<i>to get it for me. I was thankful too.</i>

2006
01:28:27,302 --> 01:28:30,263
I wrote that so he would know it was me.

2007
01:28:30,346 --> 01:28:31,514
That's why it's alphabet T?

2008
01:28:31,597 --> 01:28:34,684
-She should have written T-E-A.
-Yes, write T-E-A.

2009
01:28:34,767 --> 01:28:39,022
-I thought it was T from the MBTI.
-Me too. I thought it was that.

2010
01:28:39,105 --> 01:28:43,067
The way Hye-won expresses herself
often goes beyond what I expect.

2011
01:28:43,151 --> 01:28:45,903
<i>So I figured it was Hye-won.</i>

2012
01:28:51,951 --> 01:28:53,453
<i>It was cute. She wrote, "I like you."</i>

2013
01:28:53,536 --> 01:28:55,455
JUNG-MIN'S BOX
GA-YEON: 26, ??: 20 BLACK HEARTS

2014
01:28:55,538 --> 01:28:57,206
I could tell it was from Ga-yeon.

2015
01:28:57,790 --> 01:28:59,375
It suited her personality.

2016
01:29:05,048 --> 01:29:07,008
<i>When I first saw "IA,"</i>

2017
01:29:07,592 --> 01:29:11,095
<i>I wondered</i>
<i>what this person's intentions were.</i>

2018
01:29:13,431 --> 01:29:16,351
<i>On the first day, I did his makeup</i>

2019
01:29:16,434 --> 01:29:18,269
<i>because he said</i>
<i>he didn't know how to do it.</i>

2020
01:29:18,978 --> 01:29:20,730
Let me do it for you, sir.

2021
01:29:20,813 --> 01:29:23,024
Do you have dry skin? You do.

2022
01:29:23,107 --> 01:29:26,861
I asked him to get me
an Iced Americano instead.

2023
01:29:27,445 --> 01:29:29,364
You have to make me coffee.

2024
01:29:29,447 --> 01:29:30,365
I will.

2025
01:29:30,448 --> 01:29:32,658
You're my makeup artist. Of course I will.

2026
01:29:34,202 --> 01:29:35,912
<i>I remembered that conversation.</i>

2027
01:29:41,000 --> 01:29:42,251
I'D LIKE TO TALK TO YOU

2028
01:29:42,335 --> 01:29:45,463
<i>I wanted to get to know Do-geon better,</i>

2029
01:29:46,631 --> 01:29:48,591
<i>so I wrote, "I'd like to talk to you"</i>

2030
01:29:48,674 --> 01:29:49,759
<i>and gave him one.</i>

2031
01:29:49,842 --> 01:29:51,010
YE-RIM → DO-GEON
1 HEART

2032
01:29:51,094 --> 01:29:54,472
I felt more at ease
putting it in Do-geon's box.

2033
01:29:54,555 --> 01:29:56,265
I made that decision pretty quickly.

2034
01:29:57,350 --> 01:30:00,019
<i>But I had more Black Heart Chips</i>
<i>than I expected,</i>

2035
01:30:00,103 --> 01:30:03,272
<i>so I had no clue who did it</i>

2036
01:30:04,023 --> 01:30:06,359
<i>or why someone would do that.</i>

2037
01:30:08,152 --> 01:30:09,112
Black?

2038
01:30:09,695 --> 01:30:11,864
Why me? I don't get it.

2039
01:30:14,158 --> 01:30:17,036
<i>Why did they give them to me?</i>
<i>Does someone not like me?</i>

2040
01:30:17,120 --> 01:30:19,122
I don't like those Black Heart Chips.

2041
01:30:19,205 --> 01:30:21,499
What if you open your box
and only see Black Heart Chips?

2042
01:30:21,582 --> 01:30:22,875
Joo-heon, be honest.

2043
01:30:22,959 --> 01:30:24,877
If you didn't get any,
that would be more upsetting.

2044
01:30:25,586 --> 01:30:26,963
-Come on.
-Really?

2045
01:30:27,046 --> 01:30:29,132
"I guess I'm not intimidating!"

2046
01:30:29,215 --> 01:30:30,633
-Because you have none?
-Yeah.

2047
01:30:30,716 --> 01:30:31,759
I see it now.

2048
01:30:36,806 --> 01:30:39,225
<i>I didn't have this feeling</i>
<i>on the first day.</i>

2049
01:30:39,308 --> 01:30:41,519
But I really wanted to be king.

2050
01:30:42,103 --> 01:30:45,690
I didn't want to ask for any favors.
I wanted to accomplish it on my own.

2051
01:30:45,773 --> 01:30:47,150
Is that arrogant?

2052
01:30:47,233 --> 01:30:48,901
Anyway…

2053
01:30:49,944 --> 01:30:51,195
<i>When I read the rules,</i>

2054
01:30:51,696 --> 01:30:54,657
<i>I could cast the Black Heart Chips</i>
<i>to anyone.</i>

2055
01:30:54,740 --> 01:30:58,411
<i>and I could exchange my Heart Chips</i>
<i>for Black Heart Chips.</i>

2056
01:30:59,996 --> 01:31:01,956
As soon as I saw that,

2057
01:31:02,540 --> 01:31:06,961
<i>I wanted to be closer to becoming king</i>
<i>even if it was in terms of probability.</i>

2058
01:31:09,338 --> 01:31:11,048
<i>I guess you can call it lust for power.</i>

2059
01:31:12,508 --> 01:31:13,718
<i>So I exchanged…</i>

2060
01:31:16,721 --> 01:31:17,555
<i>my chips.</i>

2061
01:31:19,140 --> 01:31:22,393
KANG KYUNG-HO
60 HEARTS

2062
01:31:22,476 --> 01:31:24,312
<i>Some may say I'm playing dirty,</i>

2063
01:31:24,395 --> 01:31:26,856
<i>but I wanted to be king that much.</i>

2064
01:31:26,939 --> 01:31:28,316
I was that desperate.

2065
01:31:29,108 --> 01:31:31,402
TOTAL OF 70 BLACK HEART CHIPS
INCLUDING 10 PROVIDED INITIALLY

2066
01:31:32,320 --> 01:31:34,989
GIVING 10 BLACK HEART CHIPS EACH

2067
01:31:35,072 --> 01:31:38,367
<i>I was hoping I had a bit more of</i>
<i>an advantage than the others.</i>

2068
01:31:39,827 --> 01:31:42,663
<i>All participants have finished</i>
<i>checking their vote boxes.</i>

2069
01:31:54,508 --> 01:31:55,384
Did it scare you?

2070
01:31:56,010 --> 01:31:58,888
<i>Moments ago, your Heart Chip votes</i>

2071
01:31:58,971 --> 01:32:02,558
<i>crowned the second king.</i>

2072
01:32:03,226 --> 01:32:05,603
<i>Please congratulate them</i>
<i>with a round of applause.</i>

2073
01:32:11,734 --> 01:32:15,488
<i>I had no doubt that our strategy worked.</i>

2074
01:32:16,822 --> 01:32:19,533
<i>I did suggest</i>
<i>that we should vote for Ga-yeon.</i>

2075
01:32:19,617 --> 01:32:22,119
-Should we vote for Ga-yeon?
-Would that be better?

2076
01:32:22,703 --> 01:32:24,580
We were going to choose you.

2077
01:32:24,664 --> 01:32:25,748
Why?

2078
01:32:25,831 --> 01:32:27,625
-We thought it'd be better.
-When did it change?

2079
01:32:28,209 --> 01:32:30,211
Why did you want to make me king?

2080
01:32:31,003 --> 01:32:33,214
I would prefer to vote for you.

2081
01:32:33,297 --> 01:32:34,131
That was my plan.

2082
01:32:34,715 --> 01:32:36,133
-Why?
-Hmm?

2083
01:32:36,217 --> 01:32:37,468
I have my reasons.

2084
01:32:37,551 --> 01:32:38,594
I'm curious.

2085
01:32:40,721 --> 01:32:43,975
<i>If Ga-yeon becomes king,</i>
<i>she can choose her own date.</i>

2086
01:32:44,684 --> 01:32:47,478
<i>I could find out how she feels.</i>

2087
01:32:48,312 --> 01:32:49,855
<i>That's why I gave her a lot.</i>

2088
01:32:50,564 --> 01:32:53,067
JUNG-MIN'S VOTE: 65 → GA-YEON
57 → HYE-WON, 10 BLACK HEARTS → KYUNG-HO

2089
01:32:53,150 --> 01:32:56,362
Didn't he make an alliance?

2090
01:32:57,822 --> 01:32:59,198
Ga-yeon may become king.

2091
01:32:59,782 --> 01:33:02,326
If I became king,
my choice would be visible.

2092
01:33:02,410 --> 01:33:04,537
Jung-min has been openly pursuing me.

2093
01:33:04,620 --> 01:33:06,872
So if I choose him, everything is set.

2094
01:33:06,956 --> 01:33:09,500
But for me, there's Kyung-ho
who keeps grabbing my attention.

2095
01:33:09,583 --> 01:33:11,127
And Do-geon gave me hearts too.

2096
01:33:11,836 --> 01:33:13,796
<i>It would be better</i>
<i>if I didn't become king.</i>

2097
01:33:15,006 --> 01:33:16,215
<i>The power to decide the date.</i>

2098
01:33:16,299 --> 01:33:19,719
I really wanted to become king
because of that one thing.

2099
01:33:19,802 --> 01:33:22,722
I wanted to become king
and go on a date with Ga-yeon.

2100
01:33:24,974 --> 01:33:27,685
But what if Ga-yeon becomes king
and goes out with Kyung-ho?

2101
01:33:27,768 --> 01:33:29,186
Then, what about Jung-min?

2102
01:33:34,608 --> 01:33:36,152
Maybe they won't tell us.

2103
01:33:36,902 --> 01:33:38,112
Maybe not?

2104
01:33:39,572 --> 01:33:40,990
<i>The second king is</i>

2105
01:33:41,073 --> 01:33:42,033
<i>Jung Hye-won.</i>

2106
01:33:42,616 --> 01:33:44,243
<i>It's Jung Hye-won.</i>

2107
01:33:47,330 --> 01:33:50,624
<i>By combining the total of the Heart Chips</i>
<i>and Black Heart Chips,</i>

2108
01:33:51,208 --> 01:33:54,712
<i>Jung Hye-won has become the second king.</i>

2109
01:33:56,213 --> 01:33:58,007
<i>She became king as I wanted.</i>

2110
01:33:58,090 --> 01:34:01,052
The four of us did create that result.

2111
01:34:01,135 --> 01:34:04,013
<i>They must have made Hye-won king.</i>

2112
01:34:04,096 --> 01:34:07,183
The strategy of
the four people alliance worked.

2113
01:34:09,185 --> 01:34:13,314
JUNG-MIN → HYE-WON

2114
01:34:13,397 --> 01:34:15,441
HA-YOON → HYE-WON

2115
01:34:15,858 --> 01:34:17,568
HA-YOON: 65, JUNG-MIN: 57,
KYUNG-HO: 10 BLACK HEARTS

2116
01:34:17,651 --> 01:34:19,987
JUNG HYE-WON
112 HEARTS

2117
01:34:20,696 --> 01:34:23,240
<i>To be honest, I was a bit embarrassed.</i>

2118
01:34:23,824 --> 01:34:27,286
Compared to getting Heart Chips
because you're popular,

2119
01:34:27,870 --> 01:34:29,955
I got mine through

2120
01:34:30,039 --> 01:34:35,503
a lewd, manipulative
and calculated method.

2121
01:34:35,586 --> 01:34:37,671
So I couldn't just be happy about it.

2122
01:34:37,755 --> 01:34:39,256
I did a little acting.

2123
01:34:39,340 --> 01:34:42,176
You meant "sneaky"
instead of "lewd," right?

2124
01:34:42,259 --> 01:34:43,219
Oh, yes.

2125
01:34:44,678 --> 01:34:46,263
Sneaky.

2126
01:34:47,264 --> 01:34:49,266
What does "lewd" mean?

2127
01:34:51,936 --> 01:34:53,771
<i>I anticipated getting</i>
<i>some </i><i>Black </i><i>Heart </i><i>Chips.</i>

2128
01:34:53,854 --> 01:34:56,482
But I didn't expect
to get so few Heart Chips.

2129
01:35:03,656 --> 01:35:05,408
I HAD FUN

2130
01:35:07,493 --> 01:35:08,953
YE-RIM → KYUNG-HO
1 HEART

2131
01:35:09,537 --> 01:35:12,957
I didn't want to make him uncomfortable,
so I just put one in.

2132
01:35:16,752 --> 01:35:18,671
You can make him uncomfortable.

2133
01:35:18,754 --> 01:35:19,880
Make him uncomfortable.

2134
01:35:19,964 --> 01:35:21,507
I know. You can.

2135
01:35:21,590 --> 01:35:22,591
I know.

2136
01:35:22,675 --> 01:35:24,802
He's uncomfortable? So what?

2137
01:35:24,885 --> 01:35:25,886
You like him.

2138
01:35:27,138 --> 01:35:28,973
YOU'RE LIKE A K-POP IDOL

2139
01:35:30,808 --> 01:35:32,393
GA-YEON → KYUNG-HO
3 HEARTS

2140
01:35:32,476 --> 01:35:35,479
Regarding Kyung-ho,
my eyes are just drawn to him

2141
01:35:35,563 --> 01:35:37,481
and I'm curious about him. That's it.

2142
01:35:37,565 --> 01:35:40,860
It's not that I'm interested in him
as a man.

2143
01:35:41,485 --> 01:35:43,195
YE-RIM: 1, GA-YEON: 3
JUNG-MIN: 10 BLACK HEARTS

2144
01:35:43,279 --> 01:35:45,614
KANG KYUNG-HO
-6 HEARTS

2145
01:35:45,698 --> 01:35:49,368
<i>Jung Hye-won is the second king.</i>

2146
01:35:50,536 --> 01:35:52,830
<i>I had to keep a straight face</i>
<i>when the results came out.</i>

2147
01:35:52,913 --> 01:35:54,498
<i>But I bet it showed in that instant.</i>

2148
01:35:55,124 --> 01:35:59,879
<i>Her kingship stays intact</i>
<i>until the Heart Chip vote tomorrow.</i>

2149
01:35:59,962 --> 01:36:01,964
<i>I wasn't happy.</i>

2150
01:36:03,007 --> 01:36:05,468
I did think that someone else
could become king,

2151
01:36:05,551 --> 01:36:08,429
but I added some of my strategy, right?

2152
01:36:08,512 --> 01:36:09,847
It wasn't some, actually.

2153
01:36:09,930 --> 01:36:12,391
But that didn't even work.

2154
01:36:17,146 --> 01:36:19,023
This is like a rollercoaster.

2155
01:36:20,441 --> 01:36:22,735
-Is it unbelievable?
-I'm so scared.

2156
01:36:25,154 --> 01:36:28,491
<i>Now, the king's privilege</i>
<i>will be announced.</i>

2157
01:36:28,574 --> 01:36:29,867
What if it's different from yesterday?

2158
01:36:31,118 --> 01:36:34,205
<i>The second king, Jung Hye-won,</i>

2159
01:36:34,288 --> 01:36:41,003
<i>first, has the power</i>
<i>to decide tomorrow's dates.</i>

2160
01:36:43,297 --> 01:36:44,173
<i>Second,</i>

2161
01:36:44,256 --> 01:36:47,218
<i>she can choose one man and woman</i>

2162
01:36:47,301 --> 01:36:50,971
<i>to send to the glamping tent</i>
<i>for the night.</i>

2163
01:36:51,555 --> 01:36:53,724
-Yes! Yes!
-Wow.

2164
01:36:56,101 --> 01:36:57,353
-Sending them out?
-No way.

2165
01:36:57,436 --> 01:37:02,191
<i>Tomorrow's date is</i> a <i>one-on-one </i><i>date</i>
<i>arranged </i><i>by the king.</i>

2166
01:37:02,274 --> 01:37:05,945
<i>Everyone can go on the one-on-one date.</i>

2167
01:37:07,863 --> 01:37:11,325
<i>But one couple must go</i>

2168
01:37:11,909 --> 01:37:14,370
<i>on a date that costs 30,000 won.</i>

2169
01:37:14,453 --> 01:37:15,412
-Where?
-What?

2170
01:37:15,496 --> 01:37:18,290
<i>If you want to go on a date</i>
<i>with the person you want,</i>

2171
01:37:18,374 --> 01:37:22,253
<i>you must win the favor of the king</i>
<i>from now on.</i>

2172
01:37:24,797 --> 01:37:27,258
The king has gotten another privilege.

2173
01:37:27,341 --> 01:37:29,677
Then, she can decide
everyone's one-on-on date?

2174
01:37:30,302 --> 01:37:31,845
Even today's glamping.

2175
01:37:33,514 --> 01:37:36,308
I'm going to start a mind game.

2176
01:37:36,392 --> 01:37:37,393
Mind game?

2177
01:37:37,476 --> 01:37:38,936
-Don't do that.
-Why not?

2178
01:37:39,520 --> 01:37:41,981
-What?
-You will all play a mind game.

2179
01:37:42,064 --> 01:37:44,984
Whoever loses
can choose someone and leave.

2180
01:37:46,569 --> 01:37:48,153
-That's rough.
-Not bad, right?

2181
01:37:48,237 --> 01:37:49,321
I can't do it.

2182
01:37:50,531 --> 01:37:51,615
-No!
-Come on!

2183
01:37:51,699 --> 01:37:53,576
THE 2ND KING'S BULLDOZER-LIKE APPROACH

2184
01:37:55,119 --> 01:37:56,954
She's the true tyrant.

2185
01:37:57,037 --> 01:37:58,163
Excuse me. Do you agree?

2186
01:37:58,247 --> 01:38:01,208
To be honest, I'm not a tyrant
like a certain someone.

2187
01:38:01,292 --> 01:38:03,544
-I agree, Your Highness.
-"Like a certain someone."

2188
01:38:04,295 --> 01:38:07,756
But please don't think of this
as a punishment…

2189
01:38:08,716 --> 01:38:10,217
because the tent is so beautiful.

2190
01:38:13,262 --> 01:38:15,472
Why don't you join the game too?

2191
01:38:15,556 --> 01:38:17,641
I am going to decide

2192
01:38:18,392 --> 01:38:19,435
everyone's date.

2193
01:38:19,518 --> 01:38:21,604
Hye-won's eyes suddenly got intense.

2194
01:38:21,687 --> 01:38:23,439
Oh, no. I'm scared.

2195
01:38:24,023 --> 01:38:26,150
Let's keep watching. Her eyes are…

2196
01:38:26,233 --> 01:38:28,485
Three, two, one.

2197
01:38:28,569 --> 01:38:30,613
-One.
-Two.

2198
01:38:30,696 --> 01:38:31,572
-Three!
-Three.

2199
01:38:31,655 --> 01:38:32,740
Four.

2200
01:38:32,823 --> 01:38:33,824
We both said three.

2201
01:38:34,575 --> 01:38:36,243
-What?
-"Three" was caught.

2202
01:38:36,327 --> 01:38:38,829
-Yes.
-Okay, let's start over then.

2203
01:38:38,912 --> 01:38:40,873
-What?
-No do-overs.

2204
01:38:40,956 --> 01:38:43,959
I don't know. I don't have VAR.

2205
01:38:44,585 --> 01:38:45,628
I have to catch you.

2206
01:38:45,711 --> 01:38:47,963
-It's up to the king.
-It's up to the king.

2207
01:38:48,047 --> 01:38:49,923
Okay. We leave it to you, Your Majesty.

2208
01:38:50,007 --> 01:38:51,550
We'll follow your ruling.

2209
01:38:51,634 --> 01:38:52,676
She's scary.

2210
01:38:52,760 --> 01:38:54,762
Someone like her shouldn't be king.

2211
01:38:56,555 --> 01:38:57,431
<i>I think</i>

2212
01:38:58,265 --> 01:39:00,017
<i>I regretted it a bit.</i>

2213
01:39:00,601 --> 01:39:03,854
When she obtained the power
after she became king,

2214
01:39:03,937 --> 01:39:06,982
I could see that she did
whatever she wanted.

2215
01:39:07,066 --> 01:39:08,442
I was scared at first.

2216
01:39:09,652 --> 01:39:11,487
And…

2217
01:39:11,570 --> 01:39:13,030
when I say, "Three, two, one…"

2218
01:39:13,113 --> 01:39:15,032
<i>I saw her madness.</i>

2219
01:39:15,616 --> 01:39:17,159
…anyone can start.

2220
01:39:17,826 --> 01:39:21,330
<i>I sat at the end of the couch</i>
<i>and thought that.</i>

2221
01:39:23,207 --> 01:39:27,586
I'm so sorry.
I want to play a slightly different game.

2222
01:39:28,837 --> 01:39:30,673
-She's annoying.
-She's toying with us.

2223
01:39:30,756 --> 01:39:31,840
She's driving me crazy.

2224
01:39:32,549 --> 01:39:34,051
There's nothing we can do.

2225
01:39:36,178 --> 01:39:37,012
Dum!

2226
01:39:37,429 --> 01:39:38,263
Dum!

2227
01:39:38,347 --> 01:39:39,264
-Dum.
-What's that?

2228
01:39:39,348 --> 01:39:40,182
Dum!

2229
01:39:40,265 --> 01:39:41,642
-Dum.
-Du… No!

2230
01:39:42,393 --> 01:39:43,602
THE TWO THAT DIDN'T SAY "DUM"

2231
01:39:43,686 --> 01:39:45,479
-Oh, no.
-Decide with rock-paper-scissors.

2232
01:39:45,562 --> 01:39:47,564
I don't know who won.

2233
01:39:48,148 --> 01:39:49,858
Do rock-paper-scissors.

2234
01:39:50,776 --> 01:39:52,194
Or should the two of you go?

2235
01:39:54,780 --> 01:39:56,115
Do whatever you want.

2236
01:39:56,865 --> 01:39:57,908
Hye-won.

2237
01:39:57,991 --> 01:39:59,034
All right.

2238
01:39:59,576 --> 01:40:00,786
Do you two want to go out?

2239
01:40:04,498 --> 01:40:06,834
-Why is she suddenly going off the rails?
-But,

2240
01:40:06,917 --> 01:40:08,419
she knows how show business works.

2241
01:40:08,502 --> 01:40:11,255
If she became king and said,
"What do you want to do?"

2242
01:40:11,338 --> 01:40:13,173
That's no fun. A tyrant is fun!

2243
01:40:13,257 --> 01:40:16,427
It is fun, but I don't think
it's intentional. That's what's scary.

2244
01:40:16,510 --> 01:40:17,594
That's true.

2245
01:40:17,678 --> 01:40:19,930
You know, she's so rude
to the people who helped her.

2246
01:40:20,013 --> 01:40:21,974
I know. Ga-yeon helped her out.

2247
01:40:22,057 --> 01:40:23,267
Do you two want to go out?

2248
01:40:27,020 --> 01:40:29,314
-We've encountered a real tyrant.
-No.

2249
01:40:29,398 --> 01:40:30,357
So that's a tyrant.

2250
01:40:31,734 --> 01:40:34,361
Shall we talk and decide among ourselves?

2251
01:40:34,445 --> 01:40:35,821
Isn't it better than rock-paper-scissors.

2252
01:40:35,904 --> 01:40:37,489
Rock-paper-scissors!

2253
01:40:37,573 --> 01:40:39,199
No. Hold on.

2254
01:40:39,283 --> 01:40:40,200
No.

2255
01:40:40,868 --> 01:40:42,828
What's wrong? I haven't said so.

2256
01:40:43,537 --> 01:40:45,581
VOIDED

2257
01:40:47,249 --> 01:40:48,584
You're such a tyrant.

2258
01:40:50,085 --> 01:40:52,129
I've never seen a king like that.

2259
01:40:52,212 --> 01:40:55,132
Rock-paper-scissors.

2260
01:40:55,215 --> 01:40:57,301
DO-GEON LOSES

2261
01:40:58,552 --> 01:41:01,513
Then, please choose someone
within three seconds.

2262
01:41:04,433 --> 01:41:06,101
I'll take Ga-yeon with me.

2263
01:41:06,727 --> 01:41:08,103
I'll take Ga-yeon with me.

2264
01:41:16,779 --> 01:41:18,614
-This is thrilling.
-I got goose bumps.

2265
01:41:19,615 --> 01:41:20,991
I'll take Ga-yeon with me.

2266
01:41:24,203 --> 01:41:25,329
What…

2267
01:41:27,539 --> 01:41:29,583
HER HAPPINESS WAS
SNATCHED AWAY IN 3 SECONDS

2268
01:41:30,292 --> 01:41:31,794
You gloated, didn't you?

2269
01:41:31,877 --> 01:41:33,504
You shouldn't have gloated!

2270
01:41:34,129 --> 01:41:36,632
-That was such a fun choice.
-For real.

2271
01:41:37,716 --> 01:41:38,592
If I go down, you go down.

2272
01:41:38,675 --> 01:41:40,469
-He's smart.
-"If I go down, you go down?"

2273
01:41:40,552 --> 01:41:44,681
<i>I've been wanting to</i>
<i>get to know Ga-yeon for a while.</i>

2274
01:41:44,765 --> 01:41:47,267
Since I happened to lose in the game,

2275
01:41:47,351 --> 01:41:52,439
I thought I could use
going together as a cover.

2276
01:41:52,523 --> 01:41:58,821
<i>Because Chae-rin doesn't know</i>
<i>that I am interested in Ga-yeon,</i>

2277
01:41:58,904 --> 01:42:04,952
<i>and Ga-yeon was already forming</i>
<i>a relationship with Jung-min.</i>

2278
01:42:05,035 --> 01:42:09,122
<i>So I thought it turned out for the better.</i>

2279
01:42:09,706 --> 01:42:11,166
If I go down, you go down.

2280
01:42:11,250 --> 01:42:12,584
"If I go down, you go down?"

2281
01:42:12,668 --> 01:42:13,877
Nice.

2282
01:42:14,378 --> 01:42:15,504
Well, I suppose

2283
01:42:16,255 --> 01:42:17,130
I agree with it.

2284
01:42:17,756 --> 01:42:20,175
Oh, my. Tonight will be crucial.

2285
01:42:20,259 --> 01:42:21,802
This is so fun!

2286
01:42:21,885 --> 01:42:23,303
"If I go down, you go down."

2287
01:42:23,387 --> 01:42:25,764
You were my first impression pick.

2288
01:42:25,848 --> 01:42:26,807
That's why

2289
01:42:26,890 --> 01:42:28,183
I became more interested in you.

2290
01:42:28,267 --> 01:42:31,311
-Ga-yeon only has eyes for Jung-min.
-No.

2291
01:42:31,395 --> 01:42:32,896
<i>We keep meeting eyes.</i>

2292
01:42:32,980 --> 01:42:34,147
I feel like he's holding on to me,

2293
01:42:34,231 --> 01:42:35,899
<i>because he doesn't want to dump me.</i>

2294
01:42:35,983 --> 01:42:36,984
You make me nervous.

2295
01:42:37,067 --> 01:42:38,151
I can't just sit still.

2296
01:42:38,235 --> 01:42:40,153
<i>He only has qualities I don't like.</i>

2297
01:42:40,237 --> 01:42:41,572
<i>Maybe it's an opportunity.</i>

2298
01:42:41,655 --> 01:42:43,824
-A turning point?
-I won't use my brain today.

2299
01:42:43,907 --> 01:42:45,617
I think Ga-yeon is most curious about me.

2300
01:42:45,701 --> 01:42:47,035
<i>One thing goes wrong</i>

2301
01:42:47,119 --> 01:42:48,579
<i>and nothing goes my way.</i>

2302
01:42:48,662 --> 01:42:49,746
Then, give up?

2303
01:42:49,830 --> 01:42:50,664
Who'll become king?

2304
01:42:50,747 --> 01:42:51,790
Make me king.

2305
01:42:51,874 --> 01:42:52,833
Today, I'll…

2306
01:42:53,792 --> 01:42:55,168
<i>I'm worried those two conspired together.</i>

2307
01:42:55,252 --> 01:42:56,086
<i>Really?</i>

2308
01:42:56,169 --> 01:43:00,173
<i>I feel like</i>
<i>I'm casually seeing two people.</i>

2309
01:43:00,257 --> 01:43:02,801
I don't know. I just want to
go on a date with you.

2310
01:43:04,511 --> 01:43:05,345
Let's go.

2311
01:43:12,477 --> 01:43:14,479
Subtitle translation by: Ilyoung Kim

2312
01:43:14,563 --> 01:43:17,357
THE LOVE LAB
